{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks","id":153488,"title":"1001 Hunter Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-29T21:52:46-07:00","id":153488,"title":"1001 Hunter Story Hooks","content":"(Saw this was lacking!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1) Something went seriously wrong with the PC's last hunt. There was a witness that they failed to notice! The PC's know that their prey was only hiding in the form of a human, but the witness doesn't, and ended up reporting them to the police. 24 hours later, their faces appear on the news saying they're wanted for murder, and there is a reward for their capture! As if the mortal bounty hunters weren't enough trouble, the remaining supernatural creatures in the city now know the identities of the hunters. And worst of all, what will their friends and family think when they find out their loved ones are violent psychopaths?<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) There's a new huntress in the city who's methods of exterminating the supernaturals is far away from being subtle. When confronted, she says that the reason these monsters get away with their crimes is because humans don't know they exist. She plans to blow the secret and let the whole world know the truth. Now the PC's are faced with a dilemma. Do they let her reveal the truth and send the entire world into a panicked frenzy, or do they decide to eliminate one of their own and allow these monsters to continue manipulating the people to their whims?<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) The PC's all had the same mentor. He trained them, designed their equipment, taught them everything they know about how to hunt. So when he suddenly vanishes for a few months, they grow concerned and begin tracking him down. When they finally locate their mentor, they won't like what's become of him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T00:29:11-07:00","id":153585,"title":"","content":"4)<br /> A new club has opened downtown, which a very exclusive lineup. Guests seem to be picked almost randomly, out of the city's young and lively movers-and-shakers. Each nights activities leaves their participants tired and weary, without much memory of the past nights debauchery. It must have been a hell of a time too, because its almost as if the worm-out party guests seem physically <i>older...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T05:47:34-07:00","id":153743,"title":"","content":"5: Rumors out of Detroit aren't pretty. Something is stalking the city's abandoned neighborhoods, grabbing the homeless and streetwalkers and turning them into rampaging psychotics. The police have kept a lid on it, making up stories about synthetic drugs, but that won't last forever when the journalists start homing in. Worse, stories are cropping up that this is happening in other cities as well. If Detroit is the source, time to hit the Motor City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T11:22:34-07:00","id":154032,"title":"","content":"6. The Malleus Maleficarum, Agis Kai Doru, and the Order of St. Anthony are fighting each other over a shard of the True Cross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:36:06-07:00","id":154101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=153743#post153743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5: Rumors out of Detroit aren't pretty. Something is stalking the city's abandoned neighborhoods, grabbing the homeless and streetwalkers and turning them into rampaging psychotics. The police have kept a lid on it, making up stories about synthetic drugs, but that won't last forever when the journalists start homing in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's pretty par for the course for Detroit...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:38:50-07:00","id":154151,"title":"","content":"7. It turns out that the most powerful &quot;witches&quot; in town are a group of <i>really</i> good stage magicians. Only your cell knows their secret.<br /> <br /> 8. An angel arrives in town and utterly destroys the heinous cult running the show. As the only organised group left standing it seems like the Hunter's are running the show, while a power vacuum promises interesting times.<br /> <br /> 9. A prophetess of Isis is publicly performing magical healing to rekindle faith in her goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-30-2014, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T01:27:24-07:00","id":154618,"title":"","content":"10. a single member from each conspiracy or major compact is getting a letter inviting him or her (and up to four more members to his choosing) to come for a special &quot;ball&quot;, where he or she would be used as a representative of his or her organization and there they would discuss for the option to make some sort of a &quot;global alliance&quot; of all hunters in the world. No one knows who sent the invitations, and all of the organizations deny being the ones behind that. While it may be suspicious, the different leaders show great interest in the event and out a lot of pressure on the &quot;guests&quot; to go to the ball. Who is the one behind this event? Is it a trap? And why you of all the members of your organization were chosen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 05-31-2014, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T01:57:31-07:00","id":154625,"title":"","content":"11. The Brotherhood of St. Athanasius discover a Benediction petitioning Saint Barbara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T05:43:21-07:00","id":154720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=154032#post154032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. The Malleus Maleficarum, Agis Kai Doru, and the <b>Order of St. Anthony</b> are fighting each other over a shard of the True Cross.</div> </div> </div> </div>maybe instead of teasing about them, post their conspiracy write up already? I'm still waiting to see that Ivanovich you talked about, and I don't want them to join KSI21 as a Russian conspiracy which was never fully written :P<br /> <br /> also:<br /> <br /> 12) A new group of hunters has entered your turf, and they don't look friendly- especially with all of their tattoos and heavy motorcycles. They claim to seek after someone, and they are willing to reward anyone who would help them find him. The problem- according to their description, their target is your best friend. They claim him to be a demon- but you sure they are wrong. After all, you'll notice if he was replaced by a soul stealing monster right?... Right?..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T06:03:28-07:00","id":154726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=154618#post154618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. a single member from each conspiracy or major compact is getting a letter inviting him or her (and up to four more members to his choosing) to come for a special &quot;ball&quot;, where he or she would be used as a representative of his or her organization and there they would discuss for the option to make some sort of a &quot;global alliance&quot; of all hunters in the world. No one knows who sent the invitations, and all of the organizations deny being the ones behind that. While it may be suspicious, the different leaders show great interest in the event and out a lot of pressure on the &quot;guests&quot; to go to the ball. Who is the one behind this event? Is it a trap? And why you of all the members of your organization were chosen?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bilderburg Group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:04:16-07:00","id":154794,"title":"","content":"Wow.. I didn't knew that about that Group, and now I can't think about that in any other way :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:43:39-07:00","id":154824,"title":"","content":"13: Local police are struggling to contain a gang of white supremacist jackasses, which normally shouldn't be even an issue. The local socioeconomic situation is well enough that they shouldn't be able to recruit so easily. Is this supernatural, or is your cell blind to a bigger problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:19:12-07:00","id":155021,"title":"","content":"14: They call him Jeffy, the vampire slayer. A highschool student who spends his nights patrolling the city and exterminating any monsters he comes across. Sounds like a promising young Hunter, right? Well the PC's have heard disturbing rumors about the members of Jeffy's cell. Including a female werewolf named Zo, a gay warlock named Reed, and worst of all, Jeffy's in love with a vampiress named Devil, who claims to have regained her soul.<br /> <br /> It seems like Jeffy is getting a little too friendly with the very things he's supposed to be killing. How do the PC's decide to resolve this situation?<br /> <br /> <br /> (thought this up spur of the moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:59:54-07:00","id":155201,"title":"","content":"15: An ally of your cell turns out to be three goblins sharing a trench coat.<br /> <br /> 16: An elderly rabbi collapses on the street. In hospital it turns out that he has lost his wits; he's spent the last sixty years building an army of golems to march on the holy land and end the Jewish diaspora, he's somehow completely oblivious that Israel even exists. The doctors have given him weeks to live, that means you've got weeks to find a solution before an army of nearly unstoppable clay automatons go on a rampage. <br /> <br /> 17: (Athenic Church only) You were talking to Minerva through prayer when Archangel Michael attacks Minerva's palace. She went to battle, leaving you to return to your body. You have no blessings, no divine guidance and no idea what to do next. (A game I've wanted to see for a while is the Athenic Church vs an alien invasion; just so that the purely technological aliens could attack Minerva's palace when the player least expect it)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=154720#post154720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe instead of teasing about them, post their conspiracy write up already? I'm still waiting to see that Ivanovich you talked about, and I don't want them to join KSI21 as a Russian conspiracy which was never fully written :P</div> </div> </div> </div> I gave it a try and hit a brick wall; sorry. That said, don't hold your breath for Ivanovich. Like Bauldino he isn't planned to get much of a write up. I see him as quite similar to Santa from Rise of the Guardians. A fun loving Russian badass to parallel the one time we saw Bauldino on screen (like all Ghosts, his personality was frozen when he died and he wasn't a hunter until his last few days so the Vigil never wears him down)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T16:36:49-07:00","id":155298,"title":"","content":"18: (Union only) The local teamsters are making talk about striking against a certain big box store, creating the biggest strike against the retailer yet in your area. Some more politically minded members of the compact are hoping to use the strike as a cover, causing mayhem against other nationwide chains they're convinced are trying to destroy the workers. Your job: try to focus their anger somewhere else that doesn't involve innocent people getting blown up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T20:42:13-07:00","id":155413,"title":"","content":"19) The PC's have been cursed by a mage with a twisted sense of humor. Every 24 hours, the PC's turn into random animals, and the only way for them to change back without breaking the spell is to kill another human. Can they track down the twisted mage and end their curse, or will they be forced to live out their days slaughtering mortals to retain their humanity?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 20) One of the PC's was taken into the Hedge when their cell foolishly underestimated their last target. They managed to escape after spending 25 years in Arcadia, but discovered that their disappearance has lasted only 5 seconds in the mundane world. The new changeling must now struggle to hold onto their sanity after 25 years of slavery, but worse yet, their old cell members must make a choice. Do they help their damaged comrade heal from the trauma of the Fae, or put them out of their misery?<br /> <br /> (story involves a cross over with Changeling: the Lost)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-31-2014, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T10:13:58-07:00","id":155738,"title":"","content":"21) lately, strange things happen in your city- it seems like every superstition happens, terribly, for good and ill. When a black cat crosses someone's path and he doesn't spit, he is involved in a car accident few moments later. When someone throws salt behind his left shoulder, he wins the lottery. Who does those things? Is it a magic going out of control? A powerful fae? The deeds of a demon? And what would happen when someone would become a monster because of those &quot;superstitions&quot;?<br /> <br /> and selfish promotions :P<br /> <br /> 22) Your family had that clock for ages- a big horlogin covered with the pictures of crying angels. While it has always spooked you, there was never something weird about it. One day, someone knocks on your door. He claims to be a part of a company named &quot;Raziel Ltd&quot;, and that your clock isn't really yours- its the company's. A demon took your father's soul and made the clock into a part of his- and your- life. Actually, your very existence is false, made by the lies the demon made and bought from others. He tells you that he could make your life independent, but first you must give him the clock and go to the company's office with him. Would you believe him? Can you take that chance?<br /> <br /> 23) You have a ghostwalker friend. While you don't like her too much, she does help you from time to time with giving you important information. One day, she knocks on your door, begging for help- she says that someone needlessly disturbs the rest of the dead, banishing ghosts, sealing Averian Gates and even hunts down some sin eaters. Apparently, the group name themselves as the Ebony Fangs, and they are some sort of a death cult. Will you help your friend, or leave her for the dead?<br /> <br /> 24) Lately, there is a new fortune teller in town. You see her advertisements everywhere- in the newspapers, on radio, on TV. She claims that her predictions are 100% accurate. It's means that she is either a charlatan or a witch, and you and your cell decide to check it out. Your plan is making you into a &quot;bait&quot; and make her read you future. But when you come, she already expect you. She says she is neither a magician not a trickster, instead that she is simply blessed with the &quot;Vision&quot;. While it stinks up to the heavens, she says she has a good information for you- and that in three days, a slasher will show up in the city. She gives you a list of future victims, and tells you to protect them. Will you listen to her? And when the killings would start, will turn to her for help? And what will you do when you'll discover that she is a murderer by herself, part of a group who both kills and saves life in the name of a brighter tomorrow- the Pythian Oracles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T20:53:04-07:00","id":156218,"title":"","content":"25) The PC's are friends with another cell and have received some disturbing news. One of their friends was killed on a hunt. The bad news is that according to the security footage mailed to the PC's, he didn't stay dead for very long. While his cell was grieving for the loss, the fallen hunter promptly climbed out of his coffin and proceeded to massacre his stunned cellmates without any provocation. Someone or something brought their friend back to life as a Slasher, and by the looks of things, he's a Mask!<br /> <br /> Can the PC's figure out what happened to their mute, homicidal friend, or will they be left grasping at straws after being forced to put him down permanently?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T21:09:58-07:00","id":156225,"title":"","content":"26: (Malleus, Long Night) Someone, somehow, is vandalizing your church during services. In broad daylight, they're smearing excrement on the statues outside and covering the walls in blood and other fluids. Even with the police outside watching all sides of the building, the vandalism somehow moved to the roof on their watch. This is beyond a prank, this is something trying to send a message against God's house. The only clue anyone can find to what's happening is that whatever is doing it seems to have a special hatred for men of the cloth, as evidenced by images of the leader of the church being graphically killed during each incident show. How do you beat this thing, especially since it only seems to show itself during a mass?<br /> <br /> 27: Someone is going around town parading cryptids through the streets like they're party favors. Hoop snakes, jackalopes, even a bigfoot. Right now it's only a rumor, but if someone finally does get over the shock and grab a camera? Find out who's doing it, and why they think this even needs to be done at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T12:07:50-07:00","id":160127,"title":"","content":"28. Every dog in town pulls a &quot;Lassie, someone's down the well&quot;, towards the same well. <br /> <br /> 29. The monster menacing your town turns out to be a manifestation of your emotions, the ones that fuel your vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T03:43:43-07:00","id":160707,"title":"","content":"1001 seems like kind of an arbitrary number (not to mention ambitious??). or perhaps this is a scholarly nod to the classic 1001 arabian nights? if so then *wink* I recognise and appreciate the reference, fellow bibliophile. if not then uhh yeah dude that's arbitrary. regardless, my contributions:<br /> <br /> 30. ever met a parent who lives... perhaps \u2014too\u2014 vicariously through their son's prom? make sure your troupe are cool with bad dad stories brto<br /> 31. old joe, the town's most beloved hunter, says something insanely racist and the cell realises that their crusade against monsters may be problematic/allegorical<br /> 32. holy lord. somebody turned the regular zoo into a vampire zoo.<br /> 33. a fatter ephemeral version of the cell haunts the cell, outright asking them outright about like if they're such hot shit morally speaking next to the shit they're killing. just does the 'a-ok' sign to answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T05:48:18-07:00","id":160742,"title":"","content":"34: (TFV primary) Your cell has orders you're suddenly not comfortable with: A cell of domestic terrorists has sprung up in your area. Intel is frighteningly sketchy about who they are or what their goals include, but they have a lot of guns and a lot of anger at the American way of life. But intel is clear that they aren't supernatural and they aren't clued in. Command wants them taken care of simply because the people need to be kept calm and not panic over the fact that a terrorist cell so large even exists. These are regular, non-ENE individuals, and you're being ordered to kill them because they're about to do something that should make them a target of anyone else <i>but</i> the government's monster hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T12:44:59-07:00","id":161024,"title":"","content":"Flyboy, that is sweet.<br /> <br /> <br /> 35: (Sons of CuChulainn) Everyone knows that the Luxor casino was built and still is run by a mummy. Ok, most people don't <i>know</i>, but everyone who knows about The Arisen is thinking it. This Mummy has acquired the Stone of F\u00e1l, and something locking Ireland's heritage in a basement just doesn't sit right with The Hounds. The Irish Mob might be a shadow of it's former self, but it still has connections. The Sons are putting together a team of experts for the greatest heist in Vegas' history.<br /> <br /> 36: (Any religious group) Plans have been drawn for an intra-faith summit. Everyone's going to be there, not just Christians and Muslims, everyone: Shinto, Voodoo, Zoroastrians, every religion the mainstream considers legitimate is sending a top priest to talk about world peace and make press friendly statements. Since most religious Conspiracies occasionally use their monster hunters as general purpose muscle there's one or two in each delegation's security team. That means behind every mild inoffensive theologian and diplomat is a well armed, paranoid and quite possibly fundamentalist hunter. Can you get through the entire summit without violence; or worse, piss off the Coptic Church of Africa?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-06-2014, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T18:10:41-07:00","id":161293,"title":"","content":"37) Your cell took down a Leech. Hell yeah! It feels good to know you killed a monster. The thing is, her weird undead monster daddy isn't very happy about her being dead (all the way dead, not half-dead like vampires normally are). He's orchestrated the severe injury of someone close to one of you (a sibling, parent, or lover) and they're now in the hospital, in critical condition; the only thing keeping them alive is the monster's blood. He invites you to come fight him, but if he dies, so do they.<br /> <br /> 38) A group of Tier 1 hunters don't see a difference between your Endowments and the monsters they hunt, and they're pulling no punches. Will you kill your brothers and sisters in the Vigil when they don't listen to reason?<br /> <br /> 39) (TF:V only). All those tasty toys you get must cost a lot of money, and you're pretty sure the government isn't footing all of the bill. Orders come down from the top to start taking in targets alive, which you then deliver to some shady looking dudes in suits and surgical scrubs. Who the hell are you really working for, and why do you suddenly need a new handler who sure as fuck isn't one of the feds? (I've had Cheiron as a headcanon major source of funds for VALKYRIE for a while now).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T21:55:37-07:00","id":161408,"title":"","content":"40) Somebody has been going around and snatching the supernaturals off the streets. Mages, Vampires, Werewolves, Changelings. At first the PC's think it may be the work of some new Hunter group, but when humans begin manifesting strange powers similar to the vanishing monsters, they realize the truth. A group calling themselves the Next Evolution has discovered a way to artificially transfer these freaks' powers into ordinary humans without having to turn them into monsters! This kind of abominable science must not be allowed to reach the public, and the PC's have been dispatched to find their headquarters and destroy their research... ALL of it... Even the test subjects.<br /> <br /> <br /> But are these just mad scientists we're dealing with? How can somebody bio-engineer supernatural powers?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-07-2014, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T22:49:02-07:00","id":161429,"title":"","content":"41: Now you've seen it all. Some pricks are crying out that monsters deserve to be treated just like they're actual human beings. A repentant leech or private dick wizard, fine, maybe it makes sense, but they're convinced that it includes demons and zombies too. These idiots aren't just bleeding hearts, they're bleeding lives as they hold up other hunters from doing what needs to be done. The local monsters keep filling their heads with the idea that it's all morally relative. Maybe you need to bring these idiots to a vampire's club after midnight or the local demonic cult, and let them see the difference between understanding and just being a tool.<br /> <br /> 42: (Talbot Group) Something's wrong with one of the patients in your care. He's recently recovered from paranoid schizophrenia, and that isn't possible. He says he feels fine now, but you know that before he could barely function even with medication, let alone without. His family keeps saying they haven't done anything other than what your center advised, but your gut is saying this is something else. So you take one last Kirlian as he's leaving. Something is attached to him at the brain stem. And it's out in the world right now.<br /> <br /> 43: It's supposed to be a rumor; a massive demolition derby, best drivers only. The prize? A single wish, whatever the winner asks for. The losers die. It's true, you saw the &quot;preliminary&quot; racers tearing through the abandoned industrial park killing each other last night. Stories say the only way to get anything done about it is to enter. Is it true? Or is there another way to stop your town from becoming a smear on the highway?<br /> <br /> 44: The witches and werecats have reportedly made some kind of peace, and that's not what you wanted to hear. Both of their groups kept each other in check, but with a truce they can build their strength and threaten the very delicate balance of power in the area. If things reach a critical mass for either side they could go back into a conflict, and your cell in the middle of it. If you can find some dirt on who brokered the peace, it could pull the whole house of cards down in seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:39:05-07:00","id":161622,"title":"","content":"Edited the number on this, since you posted 41 as well.<br /> <br /> 45) A new vampire had come to the city. What's the problem, you might ask? He's a 3,500 year old Methuselah according to the records your organization has on him! This thing needs to be taken down immediately, but you're not even sure you're properly equipped to deal with a threat this large.<br /> <br /> <br /> 46) The brother / sister of one of the PC's had their family slaughtered by monsters recently.. The only survivor was the PC's 12 year old nephew, who witnessed the entire whole thing while hiding under his bed. The police drop him off with you until better living arrangements can be made. But things get even worse when the boy says your brother / sister told him about what you do at night, and now he wants into the family business!<br /> <br /> <br /> 47) The PC's start getting some very strict orders (the kind which questioning is NOT tolerated). They are given a name, a location, and told to exterminate the target immediately. Do not talk to them, do not spy on them, just a quick in and out job. This goes fine for about a week before the PC's have their door kicked in by armed men demanding to know why they've suddenly targeted fellow Hunters for assassination!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T17:13:22-07:00","id":164218,"title":"","content":"48) a member of your cell appears on jeopardy to win funds for your cell (it's not like this is your funding strat it just happened that way) and when you attend the filming it becomes clear pretty soon off the bat that the game is rigged by supernatural bs. one hunter has to answer hard questions while the others are in a race against time to unfuck this gameshow and bring the monster doing it to task","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T18:10:15-07:00","id":164259,"title":"","content":"(A bunch of &quot;Your friend has become a Freak&quot; Story hooks)<br /> <br /> 49)<br /> During a Hunt against a particularily nasty monstrocity, one of your cell-mates suffer a grevious injury. Miraculously, your long-time friend and companion pulls through. He has be nursed back to health, but he recovers. Unsettelingly though, after he recovers, he starts telling you of the <i>thing</i> which saved him. He explains it like an eldritch deathly whisper in the back of his mind, and a black vapor in the periferi of his vision. Acording to him, the <i>thing</i> calls itself The Hanged Man, and all it wants is to experience life vicariously through your friend. <br /> Has your friend gone mad? Has he been posessed? And if so, is the <i>thing</i> which posessed him telling the truth? Or does it have some sinister plan for you and your friend which it is yet to reveal?<br /> <br /> 50)<br /> One night not too many weeks ago, you and your cell were out hunting this freak Witch who had been kidnapping children from cross the county. You took a dangerous gambit, by staking out a kids house one night, but to your luck, the Witch strock and you tracked him to his lair. To your horror, you found the children buthered by the mad Heretic, each of their innocent little budies mangled so gruesomly that no mortal tools or hands could've ever been used. Worse still, they were arranged in mystic and blasphemous symbols all around the foul hovel, the merest sight of which buggeled the minds of you and your cell. The entire ordeal must've done a number on your cells leader though, because a few days ago, he showed up at your door rambeling about &quot;The Heavenly spheres&quot; and the &quot;High Speech of God&quot; which had been unveiled to him through what he described as a spiritual Awakening.<br /> You're not entirely certain what bothers you more. The splitting-headache that his rambeling words caused you, or the fact that children have started disappearing again...<br /> <br /> 51)<br /> When your wife died you took to drinking. It was the only thing that seemed to keep your mind off of her. If you were too busy puking in the gutters and getting kicked to the curb by bounchers, you could focus on your personal pain and humilliation, instead of the memory of all the things you two used to share together.<br /> It gradually got worse. You started seeing her on street corners, and occationally in the bars you took to, to slowly kill yourself.<br /> This did nothing to slow your self destructive habits, and you eventually fell in with a group of people whom you half hoped would kill, and if not, could atleast provide the means with which you could kill yourself. Before you had the chance however, the group invited you to a party. The special kind. That special kind of party where you're lead into an abandoned bomb-shelter, through narrow tunnels and claustrophobic passages, untill you finally enter into a grand hall, lit by candle light and filled to the bursting point with a pandemoneous crowd, all cheering in a cacophonous orchestry of noise.<br /> That special annoying kind where, chained and crying like a baby in the center of this hellish riot of drugs, sex and revelry, you see your deceased wife. You'd be overjoyed to see her, if not for the fact that your host just handed you a rock-hammer, told you to enjoy your 'gift' while gesturing to your wife, and welcomed you to the Ashwood Abby.<br /> <br /> 52)<br /> Waking up at 4am, is never funny. Waking up at 4am, because you hear crashing noises downstairs is downright unsetteling. You grab your gun and you downstairs. No petty thief will commit burlery in your home, thats for damn sure! As you reach your living room, you're met a sight that chilled you to the bone. In your living room is standing creature with the hooves and horns of a deer and claws which are digging into the throat of your daughter. Acting more out of instinct than anything else, you heft your gun and fire at the foul creature, half closing your eyes in fear and suprise. When you reopen your eyes, you're met with a horrific scene. The strange creature lies unconcious or dead on the floor, next to a bundle of twigs, leaves and dirt where your daughter used to be!<br /> You're just about to splatter that abominations brains on your carpet in sheer furious rage, when you get a better look at it.<br /> You're not entirely sure, but the creature has this quaint familliarity to it. As your gaze drifts over the pile of leaves and dirt which used to be your daughter, it strikes you. The thing looks a bit like her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T18:39:08-07:00","id":164284,"title":"","content":"53: (Division Six) Orders from on high; witches have been spotted near the local schools, and the corruption of America's youth can't be allowed. Orders are to strike only at the leader of the witch cult, the followers are just mortal dupes and idiots. It was supposed to be a simple assassination, but something went wrong. The witch cult <i>do</i> know magic, and even if it's limited they're drawing blood in your cell. Time's short, and you can't risk the witches finding out about the rest of Division Six. Local help will have to do, but there's just one problem; your cell killed several hunters over the past five years, and the local wounds haven't quite healed yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:03:35-07:00","id":165243,"title":"","content":"54: During an undercover investigation, one of the PC's visits a medium with their friend to have their fortune read. As far as the PC can tell, their &quot;gift&quot; is complete bullshit, even when she gives their friend a prediction, especially when she tells their friend that tomorrow will &quot;broaden their horizons when they wake up the next morning&quot;. So the PC decides to report nothing is amiss, until the next day when their friend calls them up on the phone and starts raving about the &quot;Supernal Realms&quot; and the &quot;Lead Coin!&quot; and says you have to check this shit out. When the PC's try to return to the medium's office, they find not only she has vanished, but the entire building as well!<br /> <br /> Your friend was just a civilian, they didn't know anything about the supernatural world or your hunting profession. So what does the PC do when they visit their friend and find them practicing death magic in their living room?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-10-2014, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:46:06-07:00","id":167440,"title":"","content":"55: Well this is great. Turns out your plan to corner those fairies just led you into the biggest dive in town, and a lot of guys with a 1% patch are staring down you and your cell. Two of them are already way too close to the door, and what's worse is that the fairy is serving drinks behind the bar. Right now all that's saving your sorry ass is the fact that the bikers don't want anyone calling the cops, but the more drinks get served by the fairy the more dangerous things will get.<br /> <br /> 56: Your position in the local police department has given you a leg up for the past few years; CSI techs rarely get called in for arrests, and the weird cases you could easily disregard to the rest of the department while your cell did the real work. It let you feel a sense of accomplishment without risking death or worse, but the salad days are closing. The commissioner wants cold cases solved, and you're in charge of uncovering just who killed a string of people you know are werewolves that were killing local citizens. Your stellar record is suddenly convincing everyone you can easily give the necessary clues to track down the killers; your own cell.<br /> <br /> 57: No one in the cell blames you for killing the kid. It happens, collateral damage in the Vigil. You watched the funeral from a distance, paid your respects when no one else could see you, made your confession to a priest you could trust. But someone knows. They're leaving the kid's toys on your doorstep every Friday. First it was his baseball and mitt. Then it was his old Gameboy. Now it's his stuffed animal. The one he was buried with. You know that priests are sworn to never reveal anything heard in confession, so that means the only people who know are your own cell. Who's decided you're the target now? And if it isn't your cell, who knows your dirty secret?<br /> <br /> 58: (Ahl al-Jabal) The prison riot seemed completely random at first, the skinheads and MS-13 members going at each other only for the guards to lose control and seal off the outside, barricading themselves in the secured sections and leaving the prisoners running rampant in the empty cellblocks. Already the prison gangs are taking &quot;territory&quot; for their own, and you found what you feared the most. A vampire is loose in the prison, and it's already killed a guard that it apparently thought was part of your cell. He wasn't, he was just on the payroll. But now you have a stealthy killer running through the prison walls, and the authorities wont' abide a riot running so long forever. Find the vampire, kill him, and act like you're completely innocent and waiting for the authorities when they retake the prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:15:47-07:00","id":168192,"title":"","content":"59: One morning <i>every</i> last hunter in town wakes up with a flier in their mailbox. Weapons! Power! Monster's secrets! Come all to the Goblin Market! By tomorrow the balance of power is going to be turned upon it's head. By mid-day the monster's know about it.<br /> Twist (Office of the Lord Stewards): Before the Goblins made their pitch the area was a beacon of stability. Hunters, supernaturals and ignorant civilians all benefited from a carefully negotiated peace treaty. Are the local hunters going to destroy that out of a chance to exterminate the supernaturals or has co-existance brought tolerance? Will the supernaturals panic at the thought of humans getting power? Can you keep the peace?<br /> Twist (Task Force: VALKYRIE): Here's how it works. The vampires run this town, they keep the other monsters down, they keep the Masquerade (yours and theirs) enforced, they only feed and take slaves from the inner city. In turn you give them the cash, weapons, and cover stories they need to keep the hunters down; every month or so you fly a drone packed with white phosphorus just to remind them who's in charge. Well guess who's about to buy knowledge of the government's involvement, half price with every weapon of magical destruction?<br /> <br /> <br /> 60: (Barrett Comission - Five Stars) The White House has publicly declared Task Force: VALKYRIE to be an illegal terrorist organisation. Instantly the Conspiracy shattered, loyal Americans turned themselves in to the proper authorities. Zealous Hunters turned off their radios, stripped off the uniforms, and became just one more group of armed private citizens hunting monsters. Veteran officers went mad, the Code that kept them stable collapsed as their self-identity was stolen from them, their units have gone rogue. The world's best armed Conspiracy of monster hunters has broken, and the wreckage is scattered all across American soil. Somebody has to clean it all up, and that somebody is the legitimate American army.<br /> <br /> <br /> 61: (Anyone with a magic like Endowment) The rumours of Witches you were following turns out to be a deep cover cell of your own organisation, and you've just put their mission in jeopardy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T13:24:33-07:00","id":168233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=168192#post168192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">60: (Barrett Comission - Five Stars) The White House has publicly declared Task Force: VALKYRIE to be an illegal terrorist organisation. Instantly the Conspiracy shattered, loyal Americans turned themselves in to the proper authorities. Zealous Hunters turned off their radios, stripped off the uniforms, and became just one more group of armed private citizens hunting monsters. Veteran officers went mad, the Code that kept them stable collapsed as their self-identity was stolen from them, their units have gone rogue. The world's best armed Conspiracy of monster hunters has broken, and the wreckage is scattered all across American soil. Somebody has to clean it all up, and that somebody is the legitimate American army..</div> </div> </div> </div>You have seen SHIELD, didn't you? :P<br /> <br /> 62. (Les Mysteres) The spirits are silent lately- dead silent. Your don't don't seem to find any of their former allies in the Shadow World, and the very few spirits you find are weak and scared. They speak about great spirit which was banished ages ago, and that now it returned and started to devour lesser spirits and mutate them to horrifying forms. Fortunately, you are not alone in battling that enemy. Unfortunately, the only &quot;people&quot; who are on your side are the werewolves named as the &quot;Forsaken&quot;, your long time enemies. Could your cell forget years of war against the shifters? Could the proud wolves accept help from those they hate so much? Or would the ancient spirit use your conflict for its own gain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T13:37:10-07:00","id":168238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=168233#post168233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have seen SHIELD, didn't you? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; and I actually found their handling of it to be borderline offensive, but mostly just lazy. Still, the final episode managed to be pretty damn cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T21:13:31-07:00","id":168587,"title":"","content":"63: A new drug has been hitting the streets. Local dealers have several names for it but mostly call it &quot;prime&quot;. The drug is mostly lost the crowd between meth, crack, and krokodil but it's starting to gain some traction with fighters and people who can't afford the good shit but want something beyond pot. The effects of the drug are that of an adrenaline rush combined with intense fight or flight response. Most crime labs and police departments chalk this up as PCP but never seem to find traces of the chemical on any drugs that they receive.<br /> <br /> Now darker stories are starting to appear. About how long term users tend to vanish but not before leaving behind scenes of claw marks and broken rooms. The scenes have confounded law enforcement but are mostly at a loss of who or exactly what happened. If asked, the addicts give a quick look of worry before changing the subject. There also has been a spike of exotic animal escapes as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:30:06-07:00","id":168949,"title":"","content":"64: (Bear Lodge) It's time, the Montana lodge has to be retaken. Five cells from five lodges have gathered in Helena, planning on how to best kill the werewolves occupying the lodge. No stops this time, the werewolves are going down. One of the men made a joke how this time it's the monsters in the middle of the woods being hunted, and that's how everyone's looking at it now.The wolves think they control the forests. By the time you've retaken the lodge, you want to see them afraid to even step outside their dens. Pick off the weak first, and watch as big bad gets sloppy in your crosshairs.<br /> <br /> 65: (Night Watch) The dealers in town don't fuck with your street, with good reason. You've known for years that the leeches love to use them as easy blood and quick bodies for a fight, but after you sent them a message with the fingers of one of their own, only the green or suicidal ones would think to go near your turf. Only this is drawing the wrong kind of attention, and local organized crime is eying your turf up as potential expansion. If you fight them, the leeches take your street. Ignore them, and the mob takes you out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T12:41:13-07:00","id":170969,"title":"","content":"66. An eccentric new consultant is being widely used by the local police department, a purported 'psychic'. Few people initially take them seriously, as they dress sloppily and seem to have no idea about <i>real </i>police work. However, that starts to come to an end as the consultant provides tip after tip to solve murders with unerring accuracy, and they lack the normal showboating that psychics have a reputation for. One of the PC's contacts (or one of the Cell themselves) are shaken when they see the psychic kneel in front of a corpse in the crime scene and seem to hold a full conversation with it, giving information no one has any right to know. Is this psychic a fraud covering their own murders, or do they have a true gift? If the latter, should they be hunted or join the hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:03:17-07:00","id":171012,"title":"","content":"67: They're everywhere. The googly eyes. Every where you look, it seems like someone plastered them on to some sign fixture, artwork, or even cars. While unnoticeable at first, now you can't stop seeing them. They're everywhere. What is causing this and by god how can you stop it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T23:00:50-07:00","id":171434,"title":"","content":"68) The selfie. No one in your cell could understand why such a thing could catch on. But then when a member goes to a party they begin to post them, mostly due to peer pressure they say but ever since then then begin to be <i>more</i> paranoid than normal. You asked them &quot;What has you so spooked?&quot; Their response: &quot;The selfie.&quot;<br /> <br /> The weird thing is that until your cell mate took one you never noticed it but then you did: the man behind him. You begin to look at others ones: the same man in each one. So you take a selfie of yourself and there is something weird in yours... he is yours in the janitor's closet at your work... where it defies physics...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","user":"Darkhunter","date":". 06-17-2014, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T11:28:06-07:00","id":171797,"title":"","content":"Inspired by Darkhunter<br /> <br /> 69) The selfie. No one in your cell could understand why such a thing could catch on. Maybe you're just curmudgeonly adults, but when you were staking out the club (pardon the pun) you noticed something. The youth were trading selfies, and no one would hang out with anyone who didn't have a good snap. A cultural defence against Vampires. Perhaps you can use this.<br /> <br /> Twist: Facebook is a godsend to the vigil. You think someone's a vampire, check for photos. But then you hear the kids are taking selfies to ward off a serial killer, has another Hunter become a Slasher or is something weirder in town?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:16:17-07:00","id":171937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=171797#post171797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Twist: Facebook is a godsend to the vigil. You think someone's a vampire, check for photos. But then you hear the kids are taking selfies to ward off a serial killer, has another Hunter become a Slasher or is something weirder in town?</div> </div> </div> </div>The internet is a surveillance state. Just more cuddly and filled to the brim with cats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:58:57-07:00","id":172004,"title":"","content":"Inspired by Shock. (Sorta, I've done something very much like this before for Hunter: Cults)<br /> <br /> 70) (Network Zero) It turns out the Internet is a tool of surveillance, but it's not the government's tool. It's not the Men in Black's tool. It's not even the monsters' tool.<br /> <br /> Since Ancient Egypt cat gods and goddesses have been watching over humanity, and the internet has made it so much easier to watch. On the one hand you'd trust Baset more then feds, on the other hand it's still 1984 stuff and you don't like the idea of anyone spying on the net. Does Tor even work against divine powers?<br /> <br /> So step one is to get all the cat pictures off the hard drive, what's step two? How do you stop a goddess? Ask nicely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T17:11:36-07:00","id":173355,"title":"","content":"71: Conspiracy theories are practically Vigil 101 for a lot of people. But you're not interested in the Kennedy family, or Princess Di, or even TWA 800. You want something no one else cares about; the Bhopal Incident. You're convinced that Bhopal was a test for someone, a way to try and clear out their enemies on a massive scale. But it went wrong, and thousands died, and will die. It's easy to ignore outside of India, but if you're right it's just one of a number of possible catastrophes. Find out who caused Bhopal, and maybe you can stop them from doing it again.<br /> <br /> 72: (Conspiracy) Nikola Tesla? Guy was a lunatic. But he was a lunatic who knew things, especially things about power. Even today his inventions still make the world sit up and wonder how they can be used. The US government essentially stole all of Tesla's work, but you think you found the central holding site for his most valuable tools and inventions. Normally going up against the US government would be suicide, but your people on the inside are going to make sure you get your chance when the guards are at skeleton strength.<br /> TFV: Your cell's been assigned to guard the most powerful blueprints and designs of Nikola Tesla, and orders are clear: Nothing leaves. You even have the authority to destroy the entire stockpile before letting it fall into anyone's hands, but only as a last resort. So of course, you're the one cell on duty when someone else decides they want what you have.<br /> <br /> 73: Crytipds aren't usually hard to deal with. Basically animals, many hunters believe that one they a few will be revealed and the world will accept them. Some are barely understood even after years of sightings. Mothman is one, and it's tearing up a sighting streak in coal country. Miners are anxious to even go out and do their jobs, and the local authorities are paralyzed. Mothman is said to be either a harbinger or bringer of disaster, and the area still has dozens of active coal mines. Can disaster be averted, and the enigma of the Mothman given even <i>some</i> answers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:33:06-07:00","id":174510,"title":"","content":"Dedicated to my writing partner from Ben's city.<br /> <br /> 74: Everyone knows Benjamin Franklin had an interest in alchemy. They've just found out he's a true master, good enough to achieve immortality. You see, Ben just got back from a bromantic sub-light tour of the solar system with his buddy Isaac Newton. Turns out he doesn't quite like what people have done with the country since he left and has formed a new political party which has a real chance of victory at the next elections. His policies are a mixture of his real life viewpoints and whatever appeals most to your group's personal tastes; they've had a while to develop and Benjamin is a lot smarter than he was before he started drinking those elixirs of intellect.<br /> <br /> So what does this have to do with Hunters?<br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum: Witch is a Witch is a Witch, but the Church <u>cannot</u> be implicated in the murder of a Founding Father.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Twist: The Pope isn't convinced that Alchemy comes from the devil. Isn't it closely related to science? It takes time to turn a Conspiracy the size of the Shadow Congregation around, but this is going to make things much harder.</div>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Quite a few of the Task Force are planning to cast their vote Benjamin's way, and a lot of his opponents are still content to let democracy decide the next president. Then word comes from above, it's not really Benjamin Franklin and a supernatural imposter cannot get into The White House. Will the players realise their superiors are wrong, or worse, lying before it's too late? And what can they do after they learn the truth?<br /> <br /> Barrett Commission: Benjamin might have founded this country, but he left to go swanning around the solar system while you poured your blood sweat and tears into keeping it standing. You don't like this new hippy crap he picked up among the stars, and you earned your just rewards for all your work and sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Task Force: VALKYRIE again: Word's come in. Somebody object's to Benjamin's alchemy or his policies. Either way, presidential candidates are under VALKYRIE's protection.<br /> <br /> Barrett Commission again: A good politician knows which way the wind is blowing, and today it's blowing due Benjamin. Now Ben Franklin is a smart guy, it didn't take him long to learn what's what in the modern political world but intelligence is only as good as the information it has to work with. He needs somebody to show him what's going on in the shadows, you need a seat where the action is.<br /> <br /> The Office of the Lord Stewards: American politics isn't part of your job. Heck, British politics isn't really part of your job. Civil Servants don't decide policy, they just implement it. Still, it makes you feel proudly British to have Issac back. Yet word has come to the Office. There's some major issues brewing in the shadows of Washington and they want a neutral party to host peace talks. Britain was a natural choice, and when Whitehall heard the word &quot;Alchemy&quot; they gave it to you. Well this isn't your first innings, peace talks are right up the Office's alley; in fact you've made Arrangements to host them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fun fact: this is the second time I've had the Stewards dealing with a major political figure returning. Last time it was King Arthur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:27:55-07:00","id":174563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=174510#post174510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Task Force: VALKYRIE again: Word's come in. Somebody object's to Benjamin's alchemy or his policies. Either way, presidential candidates are under VALKYRIE's protection.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda have to wonder what Old Abe thinks if you have him running TF:V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:31:41-07:00","id":174564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=174563#post174563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda have to wonder what Old Abe thinks if you have him running TF:V.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be his mandate considering what happened with the Secret Service Agent that &quot;protected&quot; him that night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T16:00:38-07:00","id":174669,"title":"","content":"Actually the Secret Service was created long after Abe got Booth's review of his presidency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T02:00:32-07:00","id":175072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=174669#post174669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the Secret Service was created long after Abe got Booth's review of his presidency.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Before the assassination of McKinley they were Treasury related and the President had a different group by a different name protecting him while Abe was in office.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T00:24:26-07:00","id":175844,"title":"","content":"Anyway, back to topic...<br /> <br /> 75: (Task Force: VALKYRIE, VASCU) Oklahoma City? Guess what, there <i>was</i> a John Doe II. He was one of yours, and he went off the res in a bad way. Contacts your organization had kept the truth about Doe II buried, but recently the grapevine has picked up chatter about a man matching his description planning something big in one of America's worst snake pits; Elohim City. Practically every white supremacist group in the country sends their shiniest shit to Elohim for training, and your man is here. Records on why he went of res are still sealed, and no one who knew him is able to speak about it. What was Doe II's role in the bombing, and more importantly, why do it? Because whatever excuse he might give, there's 168 empty chairs that want answers.<br /> <br /> 76: (Null Mysteriis) Something isn't sitting right with your latest research. Bluntly, it's going too well. Every test gives you the same results, every lab runs back the same numbers, and even your interns are chipper and unnervingly helpful. You know you were researching how witches were able to affect people's very probability on a whim when the lab was empty, is that what's happening? Is a witch trying to drive you insane by giving you the world's best luck for a scientist? How much longer can you live a perfect life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T02:33:39-07:00","id":175885,"title":"","content":"A little context on #75 for us non Americans please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=174563#post174563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda have to wonder what Old Abe thinks if you have him running TF:V.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;It's personal&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T05:57:31-07:00","id":175957,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma_City_bombing_conspiracy_theories#Additional_conspirators\" target=\"_blank\">75 is related to the Oklahoma City bombing in 1993.</a><br /> <br /> 77: Your group of storm chasers/hunters has a rivalry with a pack of wolves in your area. You try and capture the storms on tape, they try and appease the storms by throwing innocent people into the funnel cloud. You're sure they're actually causing the tornadoes somehow, but to convince the other hunters in the area, you need to get them on tape.<br /> <br /> 78: Nearly every Civil War battlefield is haunted. Don't look surprised, it was a modern war with classical tactics, of course there'd be a lot of angry dead. Everyone focuses on Gettysburg or Lincoln's ghost, but there's now a very disturbing story coming out of the South, near Vicksburg. Somehow, a Neo-Confederate group has found a way to communicate with and rally the unquiet dead, and in Vicksburg that means a lot of rebel soldiers that died half-starved and near-crazed against the Union. You've seen it before with ghosts, but never on this scale. There's a lot of militia movements in the US, and if they found out that someone's managed to get in contact with honest Confederate soldiers, all bets are off. Nip it in the bud, and keep the South from rising from it's graves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T06:52:35-07:00","id":175969,"title":"","content":"79: Times are hard for professionals like Tabby. After centuries of familiar work for one witch after another a dry spell forced him to choose between working as a &quot;domestic affection provider&quot; and going hungry. Exactly how Mrs. Millicant found herself at a Goblin Market is a mystery for the ages, but the lonely widow thought that hiring a talking cat was a wonderful idea to brighten the days; now centuries of occult knowledge is sitting there with only a harmless grandmother's white picket fence for protection.<br /> <br /> Variant, The Union: Forget that occult knowledge. Mrs. Millicant is the apple pie baking pillar of this community. If you can't protect an old woman from catnappers what's the point of calling yourself hunters?<br /> <br /> 80, Long Night: A group of witches think the rapture is coming, sounds good? Well not so much. They beleive that no matter how bad they are God's going to accept them if they have a pure soul, so they've been stealing souls of good Christians. Now you don't believe the Lord is so easily fooled, but they're still praying on the congregation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-21-2014, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T23:16:30-07:00","id":177711,"title":"","content":"81: A man has appeared claiming descent from Emperor Norton (google him) and has made several proclamations including that he is the rightful heir to the Imperial throne. The media is eating it up, and Norton II hasn't done anything to justify the police getting involved.<br /> <br /> What concerns the Hunters is that several supernatural movers and shakers from many different factions have been seen meeting with him. Norton's influence helps puts a stop to several supernatural conflicts, making the night much safer for ordinary people. The supernaturals really seem to like this guy for some reason, and little by little, everything seems to be just a little better in the city.<br /> <br /> Then orders come in from the higher ups of half the compacts and conspiracies in town - put Norton in a grave, no matter what it takes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T05:11:45-07:00","id":177839,"title":"","content":"82: Seven Vampires, two Werewolves, six Changelings, and four Witches, all in the last two weeks. Something is causing the number of supernatural attacks to escalate faster than is comfortably acceptable. Whatever is agitating the supernaturals needs to be eliminated before they cause a full blown riot and destroy any chance of upholding a masquerade!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 83: Three days ago, all the livestock died and the meat in the city became rotted. Two days ago all the water become polluted and undrinkable. One day ago people began to manifest disgusting sores across their body. Somebody decided to unleash the Plagues of Egypt, and you need to stop them before they decide to uncork the Plague of Death!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:21:09-07:00","id":178126,"title":"","content":"84 Null Mysteriis or Cheiron Group: You thought it would be just a quick paycheck. Some anti-vax nutters were making a lot of noise locally and the newspapers paid the closest scientists to do a short observational study to see if vaccines did cause autism.<br /> <br /> Imagine your horror when you found a strong correlation, well desperate times. There was a couple of witches you were on good terms with, and both confirmed it independantly. The vaccines were magically tampered with. Now who's trying to discredit vaccinations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T19:48:54-07:00","id":180288,"title":"","content":"85: You still don't believe it. Last night, every single other Cell in the city except yours disappeared. Even the Conspiracies are gone, in another country at the moment it appears. And now, the local monsters are rather aware of it, and why, your now one of the lucky guys who gets to deal with what happens when all of a sudden hundreds of creatures are trying to snuff you out. Hope you're ready...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:26:36-07:00","id":183607,"title":"","content":"86: (Loyalists of Thule) You found a leader of a cell of white supremacists in your area, itching to cause trouble. Well that can't be allowed. You followed him to his job, to his meetings, to his favorite bars. You learned everything about him, up to the day when he earned his red laces by kicking in the face of a homeless gay teen. You knew that the time to pull the trigger was closing, but then the man decided to remind you that you still had a conscience. You followed him to a local carnival, and watched as he played with his son, held his wife, greeted old friends as if they were siblings. The tattoos of swastikas and runes tell one story. The actions say another. Is this man so damned? Or can he be convinced of redemption?<br /> <br /> So, would anyone object to story hooks involving some of the fan made groups?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:52:51-07:00","id":183616,"title":"","content":"I've already used the Sons, Stewards and the Athenic Church. Speaking of which.<br /> <br /> 87: You wake up with an awful hangover and realise that you spent last night trying to outdrink a Leprechaun. You didn't do anything stupid did you, like offer &quot;your new best friend&quot; hospitality?<br /> <br /> <br /> (I just watched <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlg-p3RfRYY\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Gold</a>, which while a comedy is a good portrayal of how I see hunter vs faerie fight going)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T18:02:58-07:00","id":184255,"title":"","content":"88: (Section 9, Skin &amp; Bones) Your attempts to try and infiltrate the Russian anti-war movement have been stymied by a collection of witches, claiming that they are the protectors of the common people. Good for them, bad for you. They're wedged deep inside the Smolensk counter-culture, and typical methods of infiltration by your conspiracy won't work. Infiltrate the counter-culture, and find out what the witches plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:24:46-07:00","id":184936,"title":"","content":"You see, when I said fan groups were ok. I actually meant the fan groups I personally like were ok <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> J/K<br /> <br /> <br /> 89: (The Union) All you know about Russia is some cold war history from school as whatever appears on the local news. Apparently they're causing trouble in Ukraine? But then a letter arrived: Your name, your address, beneath a Russian stamp. The letter was from your old man, your dearly departed old man, but it's his writing and his signature below a message saying he's been held hostage by Russian Mafia in their mines, and an address. What's a Union man to half a world away from his friends and neighbors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T17:54:22-07:00","id":189012,"title":"","content":"90. (Loyalists of Thule, but works for anyone). A coven of witches has stolen an archive of notes from one of the original Thule occultists, a record of an encounter between the Ahnenerbe and one of the Arisen in North Africa. The men at the time considered this immortal 'superman' from an ancient Empire (an Indo-European barbarian who recieved the Rite of Return) as proof positive of their Aryan Atlantis theory. These modern witches are hoping to hunt down this creature and reawaken it into their service. You're looking at a bunch of Neo-Nazis who might have a demigod on their side if you don't intervene /very soon/.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T15:14:04-07:00","id":191722,"title":"","content":"91) You've had vampire's threaten your family, ghosts try to possess you, but somehow none of them just <i>bug you</i> like Norman. Your dull, friendly but annoying neighbour. What the hell is going on?<br /> <br /> 92) The &quot;large dog attack&quot; you were investigating turned out to be a shapeshifting changeling, not a werewolf. Then the &quot;impossible freak accident&quot; turned out to be an entire team of vampires cutting break lines, loosening safety barriers and planting hypnotic suggestions rather than a magical curse. The flying pillar of fire that blew up the museum and stole ancient Egyptian artefacts was followed back to a mad scientist's lab.<br /> <br /> Something big is going down, and it seems like everybody is trying to make sure somebody else is looking suspicious when it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T00:31:08-07:00","id":194407,"title":"","content":"93)You screwed up. The ritual worked, and the monster that everyone thought was unkillable is finally dead. Except that his 'monstrous-ness,' his supernatural powers, they didn't disappear. A few days ago, some white-collar nobody killed his jerkass boss in a manner you've seen before. An hour later, the guy was back to being plain vanilla human again.<br /> <br /> Last night, a gangbanger used those same powers to knock over a liquor store (as in 'onto it's side') and killed a half-dozen police officers before the powers abandoned him and he was shot and killed.<br /> <br /> Every three days, a seemingly random person within the city will gain the power of a dead monster for a short time.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that ancient text? Turns out, it didn't read '<i>cannot </i>be killed.' It actually translates as '<i>must not</i>be killed.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T01:18:53-07:00","id":194423,"title":"","content":"94) Most of the world spent the better part of the last 60 years convinced everything was gonna come crashing down in a rain of atomic fire at any moment. Countermeasures were put in place so that <i>if those bastards fire their nukes, then at least we can take them to Hell with us! </i>Those times are past, and with it most of the countermeasures... except one. The doomsday clock is ticking; who set it off? There's worse weapons than missiles, you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T07:26:44-07:00","id":194619,"title":"","content":"95) You've stirred up a hornet's nest. Quite literally. The local Werehornets didn't take very kindly to your organization snooping around their hunting grounds with lethal weapons. When hunters are found dead from dozens of bee stings that go straight through their body, the message is clear. <i>Leave now, or we will have war</i>!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 96) 6 nights ago, a hunter went missing. 4 nights ago another went missing. 2 nights ago, yet another went missing. Something is picking off the hunter population every couple of days. Can the PC's solve the mystery within the next 2 days, or will another victim be claimed by this creature, whatever it might be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T19:57:40-07:00","id":197342,"title":"","content":"97) A supernatural civil war is tearing the city apart. Normally, hunters would be all too happy to let the monsters take care of each other, but people are starting to notice. Last night, the first innocents were caught in the crossfire. This can't be allowed to go on. You have twice the amount of killing to do, unless you do the unthinkable; back one side and give them help to exterminate the other.<br /> <br /> Tier 1: It's a pack of werewolves and a cabal of witches feuding over some sort of &quot;energy well.&quot; You don't get it, you don't care, they need to stop.<br /> Tier 2: An upstart among the vampires is rebelling against their political structure in town, and has made a deal with the devil to pull it off - literally. The Vampire King has resources on his side, but the Infernalist is utterly unafraid of is scything through the opposition with hellish fury.<br /> Tier 3: The barrier between worlds has been torn apart, and the dead walk again; they rage against the faeries whose deals deprived them of eternal rest. Everyone knows you can't trust the fae, but the ghosts are single-minded in their pursuit of vengeance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T20:53:32-07:00","id":197384,"title":"","content":"98) Somebody unleashed the Kraken. No seriously, they unleashed the Kraken, and it's heading for your city! So far, your organization has been able to keep the news secret from the public, but if the beast isn't stopped soon, the people of <b>-City Name Here-</b> are about to see a live <i>action performance</i> of Godzilla on their city streets! Looks like you're going sailing, hope you've got enough life boats on board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:12:53-07:00","id":199188,"title":"","content":"99) There's a new hunter in town, and she's fighting for love and justice. Someone left a potent magical weapon lying around where anyone could find it, and now you've got the world's first magical girl blasting every monster in sight with her Magical Pink Fireballs of Justice (tm) without any care for subtlety.<br /> <br /> Getting their asses handed to them by a prepubescent girl in a frilly sequined skirt has left the monsters a little bewildered, but it's only a matter of time before they collect their wits and go a-hunting, and that not even counting the other hunters who have their own reasons to track her down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","user":"Quanutmshard","date":". 07-16-2014, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:23:05-07:00","id":199197,"title":"","content":"100) (Malleus Maleficarum). Someone tried to assassinate the pope. Some witch or mad scientist leapt at him during mass while ranting about freeing people from the shackles of the mind. The Shadow Congregation screwed up, which was why an angel stepped in to take your place.<br /> <br /> The Pope is safe, but can you say the same for the Church's popularity?<br /> <br /> <br /> Quantmshard, have you heard of Princess the Hopeful?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:05:42-07:00","id":199312,"title":"","content":"101) A plague is ripping through the Leeches in town, and you couldn't be happier; they're dropping dead (or staying dead, rather) en masse. But when the people who were previously preyed upon start showing gruesome symptoms, you wonder just what it is that's been killing the Vampires. [The twist: a joint effort between VALKYRIE and Cheiron has engineered a bio-weapon designed to be spread among the populace; it kills vampires that feed from them, but slowly destroys the unwitting hosts' organs. Is that a sacrifice you're willing to make? How can this bio-plague be stopped? Will you work <i>with</i> the vampires to stop this?]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:24:46-07:00","id":199345,"title":"","content":"102) Something has severely begun to terrify rival hunters in your area. One was found hanging from a tree in the front yard, strangled with his own intestines. Another had her head torn off and impaled on a metal spike in her basement. A third was eaten alive and the bite marks match up with human teeth. The twist is that everyone of these deaths was the result of a suicide, something is driving the hunters to perform seemingly impossible suicides. Now the question remains: Do you want to hunt this thing down, or get the hell out of the city before it comes after you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 103) Every hunter in the city is being affected, they're seeing the ghosts of people they could not (<i>or would not</i>) save from the monsters. These ghosts are out for blood too, claiming the hunters could have warned them of the danger but chose to keep it hidden. They mock them, asking how many more need to die before they finally blow the whistle, or the Ghosts claim their vengeance upon those who failed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:45:55-07:00","id":199701,"title":"","content":"104) Hunters from all across the city have abandoned the Vigil, seemingly without a reason. If you speak to them, they all seem a little bit dazed, and if the subject is brought up, they have no recollection of their past experiences with the supernatural and fervently deny such things exist. Who is doing this, and how?<br /> <br /> 105) The last werewolf in the city died last night, and you all went out for drinks to celebrate. Two weeks pass before shit gets before the spiritual phenomena becomes too overwhelming to ignore. The shapechangers always did like to ramble on about their 'sacred duty' or whatever bullshit, but you're starting wonder if <i>maybe</i> you were a little hasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T11:46:02-07:00","id":200301,"title":"","content":"106) (TF:V or Barrett Commission): You've done it. Not only have you defeated the Werewolves, you've also brought Freedom to the spirit world. Unfortunately you've started to notice cultural... well the dark side of the American Dream isn't pretty. You need help from somebody who understands a thing or two about art, about love, about spirits. You never ever thought you'd say this but you need help from hippies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T15:20:41-07:00","id":200440,"title":"","content":"107) The Magic Bullet, a relic said to grant omniscience to whoever uses it has surfaced in the city leading to a free for all among those seeking its power. The catch is that in order for the bullet to grant such knowledge, it has to pass through your cerebral cortex, and it's only good for one shot. As if the legions of supernaturals hunting after this thing aren't bad enough, everyone's wondering who's going to have the balls to put this legend to the test!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T11:11:34-07:00","id":202266,"title":"","content":"108) (The Union/ Any Tier 1 Cell): You admit, it probably looks bad to an outsider. But those Ordo fellas keep to animals and blood transfusions, the witches and wolfmen police their own, and Ms. Crabtree is such a sweet old lady, even if she has a weird ghost-thing stapled to her soul. But now you have sone city-slickers who are used to a more bloody vigil, and view &quot;traitors&quot; like you as no better than Slashers. Can you stop them before they ruin everything you've worked for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T03:58:18-07:00","id":203719,"title":"","content":"109) Rome shall rise again! So says the new leader of the local werewolves, a curious zealot who believes his monstrous gift is nothing less than the proof of his tie to Romulus and Remus. His charisma and absurd strength have made him the alpha that all the packs in your city look to, creating a dangerous unity among the usually infighting-prone shapechangers. He's convinced them of their nature as demigods and given them a purpose: the destruction of the Christianity that he believes killed Rome.<br /> <br /> 110) He's dead. He's a monster. He was your friend up until last week, when you watched him bite the dust. The poor bastard doesn't know what brought him back and neither do you, but you're pretty sure this isn't a friendly miracle. Do you need to put him down on principle, or are you comfortable keeping one of the enemy safe from the other cells in town? (Storyteller fiat as to whether or not he's been Reanimated, Embraced, made a deal with a Geist, or something more curious).<br /> <br /> 111) An incredibly unlikely chain of events causes a blackout in downtown <i>and</i> violent rioting in the affected areas. Monsters of all stripes have come out to do what they do without even bothering to hide themselves while normal people become savage and horrible all on their own. The hunters of the city are on triage, trying to help as much as they can with too few men and too few guns, but everyone's wondering; who set this chain of events in motion?<br /> <br /> 112) One of the player characters spontaneously uses magic during a stressful situation. This wasn't on purpose, she doesn't come from a magical bloodline, and has never studied such things; it just happened. Is the cell willing to use this new gift in the pursuit of their Vigil? What will they do when other hunters see them harboring a witch?<br /> <br /> 112b) Instead of magic, the character undergoes their First Change. They assume Gauru form and, once they change back, remember none of the incident. These blackouts grow increasingly common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:22:53-07:00","id":207595,"title":"","content":"113) Something is killing women by swallowing them whole. You know this, because you have been finding dessicated bodies who have been dissolved from head to toe by what appears to be stomach acid, if the analysis is to be believed. Their remains are a pile of bones which have been charred black and are laying in a puddle of murky green sludge, it's as if the monster vomited up the bones after digesting the meat. What kind of supernatural creature is large enough to swallow a person in one gulp, and why is it specifically targeting female victims?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T22:45:40-07:00","id":225679,"title":"","content":"114) A rash of unrelated major supernatural incidents occur across the globe and are barely covered up by those nations' governments. The time has come; the United States presents Task Force: VALYRIE's history and all of its collected information to the UN Security Council, demanding that something be done about it.<br /> <br /> 114a) That's when the Russian representative throws a folder down on that wonderful <i>Dr Strangelove</i> table, stuffed to bursting with documents and correspondence that show, without a doubt, that VALKYRIE is firmly under the control of vampire infiltrators who may well have the entire US government compromised. In a desperate attempt to save face, VALKYRIE is immediately disavowed, the current agents left out in the cold and hunted by the nation they fought so hard to protect. The people who've kept America safe are now branded terrorists and denied the resources they're used to having.<br /> <br /> 114b) That's when the other Security Council nations sheepishly admit that they've known for awhile, and taken their own unique measures to deal with it. A top-secret resolution is passed to consolidate the international sanctioned monster-hunting forces and turn them into a super organization with all the world as their designated territory. When an obscure wind god awaken to cause trouble all throughout the Arctic Circle, when a <i>jihadi</i> group shows implausible success and their undead patron is revealed, when a freak storm knocks the power out in a major metropolis and the rats come out to feast... that's when the Men In Black show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T19:56:13-07:00","id":227546,"title":"","content":"115) One of the Loyalists of Thule has hacked into The Union's message board, and he doesn't like what he sees. Word is soread among the Loyalists of a &quot;militant v\u00f6lkisch hate group with chapters across America&quot; using the Vigil as a cover for their unseemly activities. It's war between two Compacts, and The Union doesn't even know why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:33:30-07:00","id":238372,"title":"","content":"116) local thugs are vanishing. That doesnt seem like a bad thing, but they are people still. Eye witness testimony says they all went missing while hanging around a sewer entrance underneath an overpass...the one with strange rune looking things spray painted over its opening. The opening is a door, a door to (insert splat specific otherworld here) and these local toughs were just too close to pass up on grabbing. Can the cell close the door? Does it need closed? Whats on the other side? Do stories like this from all over the country all link to secret doors to netherrealms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:48:38-07:00","id":238561,"title":"","content":"117) People often say politicians are blood sucking monsters. Well it turns out that may be more than just a metaphor. As election day begins to approach, it looks like the next president of the USA is going to be a third party representative, a member of a Hunter cell intent on taking back the country from the undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T22:28:07-07:00","id":238864,"title":"","content":"118) (Tier One) It just happened so fast. You've found out that not only the supernatural exists, but that your best friend is one. More than that, he's being hunted by people claiming he's demonic, or something, and needs to be killed. Can you protect him? What does it mean to do that though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T13:02:31-07:00","id":240551,"title":"","content":"119) Long Night (maybe the MM or anyone): It's Job: the Sequel. God and the devil have a wager. The Devil may send his minions against you (demons are free to manifest without the usual restrictions) and those closet to you - he's not aloud to kill or maim you personally but anyone else is fair game. You can fight back of course, but good luck with that. At any time you can end it just by asking, but the longer you hold out the less power the devil will be permitted for the next thousand years.<br /> <br /> You don't know this, all you have is God's command to stay strong, and faith. Though perhaps you'll figure it out, you have read the Bible.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Feel free to minmax. God chose <i>you </i>for this wager, so a Willpower 9-10 makes sense).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:14:07-07:00","id":243253,"title":"","content":"120) &quot;In 2012 a crack TF:V unit was sent to prison by a military court for a crime they didn't commit.&quot;<br /> <br /> You know you want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:23:51-07:00","id":243260,"title":"","content":"121) Something has gone very weird. Immortals are hunting each other down and cutting their heads off. Now ordinarily this would be perfectly fine, but some of these deaths have a strange message written in the victim's blood. &quot;There can be only one!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> 122) The cell found a mirror that when spun around, changes the bodies of any two people looking into it. Well they decided to dick around and swap bodies for fun. So when the mirror is stolen before they have a chance to change back, the hunt is on for the thief. But if the mirror is destroyed, they might never be able to return to their true selves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T18:09:09-07:00","id":243509,"title":"","content":"123) You've heard of Slashers, but never thought you'd be fighting a whole cell of them. You've also heard of Cults, but never thought that your town could be run by one. And you've heard of Hunters having to work with the monsters, but never have you thought you'd need to do it against other human beings. But now, you have a mutual enemy, and even the Werewolves are willing to cut a deal now. Are you willing to take their offer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T21:18:25-07:00","id":244492,"title":"","content":"124) People are reporting strange sights and missing time, waking up with strange scars on seemingly random parts of their bodies. It would be a case of either mass hysteria or a huge surge of UFO activity, were it not for every single fucking person having a different story of what happened. It's time for a delicious &quot;what the hell really went down?&quot; mystery episode. (I'm inclined to have the monster be a vampire with memory-altering powers and a love for old conspiracy theories).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T01:13:17-07:00","id":245942,"title":"","content":"125) The Loyalists of Thule tried transporting ancient occult scrolls through the city, unfortunately the vehicle transporting them was involved in a road accident, the death of those nearby was enough to awaken the creature locked within the ancient scrolls, the PCs must now hunt down a creature that grows more powerful the more it kills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T07:36:23-07:00","id":246796,"title":"","content":"126) (Union) Yeah, you want to defend the community and all that fun jazz, but what do you do when its clear the police are either Vampiric or in the control of them? Or when Werewolves make up most Firefighters? The Vampires you've linked to multiple murders recently, and are clearly covering up other shit, but what are you going to do about it? Murder the local police?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T23:58:21-07:00","id":247544,"title":"","content":"127) Your cell discovers vital information on the cities *insert monsters of your choice* and their human followers are being stored in a safety deposit box in the center of one of the cities largest banks. Your cell has to retrieve this data, but that would mean becoming bank robbers and taking on the city's police force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":3786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","user":"LeicsFox","date":". 03-05-2018, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T23:03:39-07:00","id":248620,"title":"","content":"128) It was a brutal battle, but you came out on top. There's one last thing you have to deal with - disposal. Your cell doesn't have the know-how to make sure this thing stays in the grave, but your contacts tell you of a generally amicable (insert supernatural/hunter of choice here) who has the resources you need. You just have to get to him before the next full moon.<br /> <br /> You'll have to avoid loyal cultists who want their master back, other hunters with their own plans for such an unusual corpse, attention from mortal authorities, nosy tourists, and everything else life decides to throw at you for the next couple of weeks.<br /> <br /> Road trip!<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> &quot;We can't stop here. This is werewolf country.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T23:16:41-07:00","id":248632,"title":"","content":"129) One of your cell members has a sibling. This sibling has become (insert monster here) and has grown to revel in their new power. Your cellmate has taken this quite personally and now the sibling rivalry has turned into a full blown war that only one of them will survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T07:04:37-07:00","id":249759,"title":"","content":"Shapeshifter themed stories!<br /> <br /> <br /> 130) Those damnable Werepidgeons have insulted your cell's leader for the last time when they shat all over his daughter's brand new car. Time to cull the flock!<br /> <br /> <br /> 131) Somebody killed Bambi's mom, and now the Weredeer are out for blood!<br /> <br /> <br /> 132) Afraid their son might develop abandonment issues without their parent around, one of the cellmates gets them a pet dog. But when this dog turns out to be a skinwalker, it's time to stage an &quot;accident&quot; without the boy knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-05-2014, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T06:43:13-07:00","id":250725,"title":"","content":"133. A mysterious cult is killing mortals all over town in a ritualistic manner. It seems like the locations are specifically picked and the murders are carefully planned by this group. Is this just a cult of serial killers? Or are the murders just a means to an end? <br /> 134. When you and your group take the subway to downtown something weird happens. You experience loss of time and you end up in a rusty subway train in an abandoned subway station. It appears that part isn't used for years. What happened here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","user":"Jan Paparazzi","date":". 09-06-2014, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:12:53-07:00","id":250736,"title":"","content":"135. Your cell or an allied cell catch a civilian in the crossfire of a hunt. The body disappears mysteriously and someone who looks an awful lot like the freshly dead innocent bystander starts making trouble for the people responsible for their death.<br /> <br /> 136. Who knows what evil lurks in the hearts of man? This new guy claims to be able to smell sin and evil on a person, and they seem to be legitimate. So far, at least...<br /> <br /> 137. There is a clown haunting your city. They've not done anything, and they've been captured on film by several sources, but there's something decidedly... off about them.<br /> <br /> 138. Your cell hears word of a new black market source for all source of anti-supernatural gear which actually work, but the prices are rather esoteric. Vampire blood gathered under a full moon. The last breath of a child. The memory of your first love...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T17:16:18-07:00","id":251775,"title":"","content":"139) There's this old pizza joint that's quite popular among children because of the lifelike animatronics that work there. The cell has heard interesting stories about how the place is having difficulty hiring night watchmen for longer than a week at a time before they either quit... or vanish without a trace. It's time to go under cover and find out what's causing the employees such problems, and put a stop to it if it proves supernatural in nature!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/SJdkeDxkqAQ\" data-code=\"SJdkeDxkqAQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SJdkeDxkqAQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-07-2014, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T18:40:13-07:00","id":256940,"title":"","content":"140) The ancient pagan religions were on the cusp of finding a way back into the supernal realms before they were driven to extinction by the Templar crusades. Whether the Hunters know about the realms is not important. What is important is that a cabal of time traveling mages hopes to ensure the crusades never happened... they plan to assassinate Jesus before Christianity is ever founded. Fortunately for the Hunters, the government has a time traveling machine to deal with threats such as these. Can they stop the mage's dark plans, or will one of the world's most powerful religions (and organizations based on it) be snuffed out in the blink of an eye?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T13:30:55-07:00","id":257536,"title":"","content":"I'm betting that Yeshua ben Yeshua uses his awesome Jesus Powers to defeat the Mages without trouble, and this attempted assassination creates a stable time loop that's responsible for the crusades.<br /> <br /> Hubris + time travel, you were all thinking it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (yes I know the Old Testament said some things about witchcraft, Jesus did cross out parts of the OT)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T19:33:52-07:00","id":263344,"title":"","content":"141) Modern pop culture has idolized the supernatural world. Stories that once invoked terror in your ancestors now spark admiration and curiosity among the youths of today. So when the monsters decide to announce their presence, this poses a major problem to hunter conspiracies world wide. Mages, Werewolves, Vampires and Changelings have all made their presence known and are disturbingly increasing their popularity with each passing week.<br /> <br /> How will the Hunters continue on now that the public knows their prey exists? Sure, there's going to be a chunk of the population who still fears and hates the monsters, but there is also a chunk who welcomes them with open arms. Many young and impressionable youth are lured to the supernatural by ambitions of power and freedom, or simply because they mistake the books and movies for the real deal. But then the real bomb shell hits, when the monsters announce on a global broadcast that the government has known about their existence for decades, and chose to keep it quiet from the people...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-14-2017, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T13:31:29-07:00","id":264085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=263344#post263344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">141) Modern pop culture has idolized the supernatural world. Stories that once invoked terror in your ancestors now spark admiration and curiosity among the youths of today. So when the monsters decide to announce their presence, this poses a major problem to hunter conspiracies world wide. Mages, Werewolves, Vampires and Changelings have all made their presence known and are disturbingly increasing their popularity with each passing week.<br /> <br /> How will the Hunters continue on now that the public knows their prey exists? Sure, there's going to be a chunk of the population who still fears and hates the monsters, but there is also a chunk who welcomes them with open arms. Many young and impressionable youth are lured to the supernatural by ambitions of power and freedom, or simply because they mistake the books and movies for the real deal .</div> </div> </div> </div>I've spent a lot of time thinking about monsters out in the open, I tried to run a world of darkness revealed chronicle, but that fell through when half the group moved away, so I stripped all the WoD specific elements out of what I had planned and recycled it as a novel I'm writing. So while I have a lot of supernatual stuff in the open ideas, I'm not sure how useful they would be to you guys because when I stripped the Wod stuff out of the chronicle turned novel and made my own setting for it, I also added a bunch of my own stuff and stuff from folklore that doesn't fit with the Wod as written.<br /> <br /> That being said<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to make this bad for the hunters, make a anti-hunter compact based off a group like the southern poverty law center or the anti defamation league. a bunch of civil rights lawyers that hunt monster hunters through the legal system.<br /> <br /> maybe have those lawyers represent a monster a PC hunter maimed at one point (or a coterie/pack/cabal/whatever mate of a monster the PC killed).<br /> <br /> maybe have a hunter PC's kid find out what their parent has been up to from our civil rights for monsters group's website and react with horror and anger due to her having a cute monster boyfriend.<br /> <br /> better yet, have the PC's kid decide she wants to BE a monster, even if it means having to testify against and/or kill their parent to get the other monsters to trust them. ( these last two ideas come from my novel's version of the van helsing family, who've degenerated into a massive collection of westboro style fail)<br /> <br /> meanwhile, the hunter PC's other kid gets beaten up at school by a pack of teenage werewolves who then use the PC's identity as a hunter to claim self defense in court... and it works<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-23-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T13:47:27-07:00","id":264093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=264085#post264085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've spent a lot of time thinking about monsters out in the open, I tried to run a world of darkness revealed chronicle, but that fell through when half the group moved away, so I stripped all the WoD specific elements out of what I had planned and recycled it as a novel I'm writing. So I have a lot of Wod revealed ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you really wanted to make this bad for the hunters, make a anti-hunter compact based off a group like the southern poverty law center or the anti defamation league. a bunch of civil rights lawyers that hunt monster hunters through the legal system.<br /> <br /> maybe have those lawyers represent a monster a PC hunter maimed at one point (or a coterie/pack/cabal/whatever mate of a monster the PC killed).<br /> <br /> maybe have a hunter PC's kid find out what their parent has been up to our civil rights for monsters group's website and react with horror and anger.<br /> <br /> better yet, have the PC's kid decide she wants to BE a monster, even if it means having to testify against and/or kill their parent to get the other monsters to trust them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm watching a recorded session in the Requiem universe. In their setting, there was something about a vampire who went back in time and altered something, and now vamps can walk in the daylight. They exposed themselves and all other supernaturals, and now the story takes place in a world where supernaturals walk around in the open. Some vampires (and humans) did not like this idea, becoming Rebels who wish to see the world go back to the way it was before. Currently in their story, the rebels provoked a riot, and Changelings tricked the Military into deploying the special forces to clean up the area. The &quot;special&quot; forces are a pack of Werewolves in black ops gear... Lots of delicious chaos all around!<br /> <br /> <br /> The rebels work together sometimes as an alliance of convenience. Vampires don't like being exposed to mortals, and mortals don't like feeling inferior to the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T14:06:43-07:00","id":264104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=264093#post264093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm watching a recorded session in the Requiem universe. In their setting, there was something about a vampire who went back in time and altered something, and now vamps can walk in the daylight. They exposed themselves and all other supernaturals, and now the story takes place in a world where supernaturals walk around in the open. Some vampires (and humans) did not like this idea, becoming Rebels who wish to see the world go back to the way it was before. Currently in their story, the rebels provoked a riot, and Changelings tricked the Military into deploying the special forces to clean up the area. The &quot;special&quot; forces are a pack of Werewolves in black ops gear... Lots of delicious chaos all around!<br /> <br /> <br /> The rebels work together sometimes as an alliance of convenience. Vampires don't like being exposed to mortals, and mortals don't like feeling inferior to the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really neat. Please give me a link.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T14:46:07-07:00","id":264143,"title":"","content":"Here's the first video. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4CrbxbB959E\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4CrbxbB959E</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm almost done with the 3rd video. These things are 3 and a half hours long! ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-23-2014, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T12:06:01-07:00","id":265621,"title":"","content":"(142) The Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York City is unveiling a new exhibit called &quot;Secrets of the Templars&quot; in cooperation with the Vatican.<br /> <br /> The exhibit has on display several Templar artifacts, including a strange typewriter-like device that dates back to the First Crusade, which was recently discovered in a sealed vault beneath the Vatican Library.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just as the doors are about to open, a group of seven men on horseback dressed as Templar knights ride out of Central Park, and begin walking their horses up the steps of the museum right in front of the gathered crowds of media and spectators. At first people are cheering, thinking it is a publicity stunt by the museum and Vatican. But then when a security guard tries to stop the men from riding their horses through the front doors of the museum, the lead rider draws a sword and slashes him down, while the other six riders produce micro-uzis from beneath their cloaks and open fire, gunning down security guards, police, and spectators alike<br /> <br /> They crash through the doors, and he lead rider dismounts and smashes open the display case, lifting the typewriter like device above his head and reciting an ominous-sounding Latin chant.<br /> <br /> He remounts, and the riders (some of them with human shields pulled from the crowd) gallop back out the doors and down the steps spraying bullets as they go, before vanishing back into the shadows of Central Park.<br /> <br /> (based on a book called <i>Knights of the Red and White)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2745-marrik","user":"Marrik","date":". 09-25-2014, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2745-marrik","name":"Marrik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T17:27:23-07:00","id":269622,"title":"","content":"143) Binge eating makes you lose weight, the greedy face unparalleled lucky streaks at the gambling table, murders go uninvestigated, pride comes before great success, and slacking off causes someone else to do your job for you while you still get credit! Someone or something is causing people's vices to turn beneficial, rather than dangerous and its up to your cell to figure out the cause. Because who knows what might happen to the city when it figures out life has no consequences!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-29-2016, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T18:14:06-07:00","id":281763,"title":"","content":"144) What do you when the kids have made deals with the local Witch? And not out of fear, but... love. She doesn't lie to them, and unlike their teachers or parents, is always there when they want a shoulder to cry on. She even brings them Christmas presents ever year. All she asked in return was that, if ever someone came around wanting her dead... they stand by her. Would you go through them just to kill someone for using magic?<br /> <br /> 145) (Malleus Maleficarum) All the faithful have been following the words of... a Demon. Or at least, that's what you're told he is. But if he's a Demon, why does he protect his flock so fiercely from other Demons? Or for that matter, why would he hunt the Vampires down the street? Is there something you aren't being told? And why this focus in all his preaching about not being fooled by demonic trickery? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T20:49:17-08:00","id":315046,"title":"","content":"146: You broke down the door, but no one was there. You kicked out the windows, but the second floor was clear. You started a fire, but the fire department never found any body. He wasn't a witch, fairy, ghost, nothing but someone your cell needed answers from. So how'd he escape?<br /> <br /> 147: (Malleus Maleficarum) The pope has decided that he'll be coming to Philadelphia. You have one year to prepare the city for his arrival. Ally with any hunter who's willing to work alongside you, and pacify those that won't. Ensure that when the Holy Father comes to the City of Brotherly Love, he will be safe from those that would attack St. Peter's heir.<br /> <br /> 148: You know that game that just got released? The one that was supposed to show a very conspiracy filled version of history? Someone decided the publisher and developer were revealing truths that hit a little too close to home. They sabotaged development, and as of now only one unaltered version of the game remains that could answer a lot of questions. Find that single unaltered copy, and the conspiracy's secrets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T00:09:27-08:00","id":322483,"title":"","content":"149: Cats are a mixed bag in folklore. Some cultures revile them, others treat them as minor deities. Which stories are true? You'd better find out, because a new cult in the area is killing all the cats they can find without giving a reason, and a lot of families want payback for losing their pets.<br /> <br /> 150: The local vampire lord is dead, and for a short time things were awesome. But now things are getting worse than before. It turns out that vampires prefer a power structure to run things, and by killing the grand poo-bah, you've opened up a vampire turf war for blood slaves and money laundering. As distasteful and against everything you stand for as it is, you need to accomplish the unthinkable. Find a vampire with a backing, and help him take control of the city before it's too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T11:23:27-08:00","id":322994,"title":"","content":"151: Something really powerful, obviously supernatural and visibly terrifying is stalking your town. Fortunately it has one of the most broad Banes you've ever encountered, it will die if it's ever attacked by someone who does not believe in the supernatural. The catch is that they have to intentionally attack, you can't just give them a gun and a blindfold.<br /> <br /> So you need to find someone who's mental filters against the supernatural are so strong they can look at this thing and still disbelieve it, but who you can convince to pull the trigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T12:27:48-08:00","id":323068,"title":"","content":"152): Your cell is one of the few who knows about the True Fae and how they abduct mortals and turn them into monsters. Well recently there's been a new Fae in town who offers his victims bribes in exchange for coming back home with him. These bribes appear to be magical rings, from what your cell has been able to determine. The Fae has given out 9 rings of power so far to the men of the city. Can you find and stop him before he takes another prisoner?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-26-2014, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T21:14:12-08:00","id":324198,"title":"","content":"153: &quot;You're sure we have the right time and place? What if it's a trap?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Since when can a bunch of zombies set a trap?&quot; - Found on a reanimated corpse in Detroit<br /> <br /> 154: Some werewolves don't want to be werewolves. They just want to live in peace, have a family, maybe watch the game on the weekend. Unfortunately, your cell has a problem with one in your town. Specifically, the werewolves who want to conscript him, and the zealots who want to kill him. He's clearly an innocent man and don't want any part in whatever is going on in the world. Can you turn the two foes against one another? Or will someone have to make a sacrifice for the good of everyone else?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T22:28:53-08:00","id":324226,"title":"","content":"155: (MM or Long Night) There's a monster that can strip the religious and moral beliefs of whoever it gets into contact with for one hour. Entire congregations have dwindled away as people in mass lose their beliefs. What creature is doing this? And more than that, who could stand against it? Someone with no beliefs to lose? And how do you spot this entity without succumbing to its effects too? It does seem to strip Hunters of their memories relating to the supernatural in the same package. <br /> <br /> 156: (Task Force Valkyrie): There's a mole. You don't know who they are, or who they are working for, but team after team is getting utterly butchered by the monsters specifically preparing for their arrival. The casualties are getting to the point that Task Force Valkyrie will have to halt all operations until the mole is found. But... what will happen on American soil without the presence of Task Force Valkyrie? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T17:48:30-08:00","id":325673,"title":"","content":"157: Local firefighters are being picked off on the job, being caught in burning buildings or dying from their hoses malfunctioning and pummeling them. Local departments keep saying it's all tragic coincidence, and that they're taking greater steps to ensure the safety of their men. You know that someone is looking to kill all the firefighters for a reason.Two questions: Why, and how do you stop them?<br /> <br /> 158: For some reason, aliens from outer space are not a focus of the vigil, despite the absolute necessity of the fact that hunters need to expect <i>anything</i>. So why does it feel like hunters like to forcefully ignore alien abductions with claims of the fae, or other dimensions, or even the freaking government? Why doesn't anyone want hunters talking about UFOs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T18:02:26-08:00","id":325676,"title":"","content":"Probably because UFO's aren't supernatural and hunting them would cause an interplanetary war? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 159: A Cabal of witches have come up with a ritual that enables them to combine all their magic into a single individual for a limited time. From what you've been able to gather, they plan to combine over a dozen witches into their leader, who will then proceed to exterminate the hunter population from the city. Fortunately, the ritual can only be performed during the eclipse, which isn't scheduled for another month. You have to find this cabal and stop their recruiting, as well as their ritual!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 160: A member of your cell has a problem... Something keeps leaving them presents along with love letters. That's not so bad, except the presents are in the form of dead animals including frogs, birds, rats, and house cats!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T21:07:32-08:00","id":326615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=325673#post325673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">158: For some reason, aliens from outer space are not a focus of the vigil, despite the absolute necessity of the fact that hunters need to expect <i>anything</i>. So why does it feel like hunters like to forcefully ignore alien abductions with claims of the fae, or other dimensions, or even the freaking government? Why doesn't anyone want hunters talking about UFOs?</div> </div> </div> </div>One word: Fae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T21:22:58-08:00","id":326630,"title":"","content":"161: Someone is spreading false stories to rookies in your area. Telling them silver nitrate can kill any werewolf, that zombies aren't as dangerous as movies say they are, that vampires can be killed with a cheap battery-powered UV light. It's getting people killed or worse, you only found out because you captured a recently turned vampire who begged for death. He said before he was ashed that it was, &quot;the man with the black eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> 162: The Dead Kennedys weren't wrong, football has started to get creepily cult-like. Your investigation into the local high school confirmed it when you saw the boys bleeding themselves over a football chanting for victory. If this is a cult phenomena, the scary question to ask is, how far has it spread in the sport?<br /> <br /> 163: The local cops didn't ask too many questions, and your cell has always been cautious enough to keep most answers to yourselves. Then some cub reporter looking to cut his teeth and get set for prime time decides to start raising hell about all the unsolved &quot;disappearances&quot; in the town. The police are starting to feel the public asking questions, and they're up against the wall to find a reason they've been so ineffectual. Should you back down and risk the town falling out of your control? Or does this reporter need to learn not everything is newsworthy the hard way?<br /> <br /> 164: (Silver Cross, Skin and Bones) One of your clinics in Cleveland called; there's something spreading through the vampires, and so through anyone they bite. They've narrowed it down to a strange inverse of hemophilia, tentatively titled &quot;hemophobia&quot;; when the skin is cut, the clotting is so severe that it can threaten to block vessels in the body. You're being brought on as a kind of on-site triage team. Find patient zero no matter their state of life or death, and figure out what the hell happened to the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T22:58:17-08:00","id":326673,"title":"","content":"165: Many supernaturals live in fear of the possibility that if mortals ever rallied against them, they could be wiped out. Well your organization finally got wise of this and are planning to do just that. They're stock piling weapons and resources for an all out war against the freaks who think humanity is their plaything! But not all within the organization support this idea and believe countless people will be caught in the cross fire. So the question is, which side will your cell take in the coming war?<br /> <br /> <br /> 166: Someone has infiltrated the organization for the past several months and been killing officers and other high ranking members. You've finally discovered the culprit is a body snatcher, who's been using their immortality for assassination contracts. When the killer could be anyone, you can't afford the luxury of trust. So how do you catch this assassin before he destroys your organization's chain of command?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-29-2016, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T01:01:29-08:00","id":326719,"title":"","content":"167: Sometimes, even hunters have moments of good luck. You won the lottery, or maybe a plane ticket, a weekend getaway, whatever. But after you've arrived at the resort and checked your bags, you start to notice little things about the other guests - habits, tics, body language...then it all comes together when you recognize another hunter. In fact, all the guests are hunters, from no-name cells who've just become aware of the supernatural to conspiracy bigwigs.<br /> <br /> And then the lights go out, the escape routes get closed off, and the killing starts.<br /> <br /> Someone went to a lot of trouble to get you all to an isolated location, away from your support and your armory. But you're a hunter. You've been in tough spots before. Sure, most of the hunters here hate each other, but you all hate monsters more, so just give the crowd one good speech to get them into the mood and you'll all be raring to go a-slaying!<br /> <br /> ...Assuming that the killer isn't one of the guests.<br /> <br /> ...Or that some the guests decide this is the perfect opportunity to settle some old scores. <br /> <br /> ...Or assuming that someone planned this. Coincidences do happen. Maybe all you need to start a bloodbath is one fatal accident and a lot of paranoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:47:49-08:00","id":327142,"title":"","content":"168: Mummies, freaking mummies. Not only are they real, they're greedy bastards. It's why the local museums are reporting that they're losing exhibits in blatant smash and grabs. The local fairy grapevine says it's centered around a cult worshipping a &quot;prince of a lost kingdom&quot;. For once, Hollywood just might help, because there's only one suspect when it comes to a description like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T14:22:54-08:00","id":327368,"title":"","content":"169: Dodging traps, looting temples, it's just another day for the Ageis Kai Doru. Well not so fast. This is a lost temple of the Ageis Kai Doru.<br /> <br /> 170: (Task: Force VALKARIE): You got a call from a naval officer stationed near Somalia. It turns out these pirates weren't quite human, actually they're changelings. They're acting like they're straight from a swashbuckling pirate film, and the world's playing along. When one pirate managed to escape 10 trained marines with their wallets and the female officer's phone number by swinging on chandeliers they realised they need help. FORT is insisting that their magic specifically targets upstanding soldiers and law enforcement, the only options are massive overkill or for VALKARIE to reply with it's own misfits. But VALKARIE doesn't have lovable rogues, it has war criminals, psychopaths and the Geneva Convention violating scum of the Earth. Better that than massive overkill right?<br /> <br /> 171: (Ascending Ones): Politicians are being found dead of mysterious diseases. On the streets preachers are spreading like wildfire, each claiming that Allah has sent his sword to punish those who have sold out the common people. As chaos spreads the people you've sworn to protect are beginning to suffer. Little do you know the group responsible is the Ascending Ones, armed with alchemical posions and elixirs to induce religious visions a branch of the Knife of Paradise has decided to reshape society. Not a rogue branch either, the Ascending Ones communication links aren't perfect and you never got the word.<br /> <br /> 172: Sin-Eaters like the big parties, Mardie Gras, Carnival, but not as much as they like their own exclusive gatherings. That's why they come every year to your dying city (what other kind for Sin-Eaters?) to party like they die tomorrow. It's not like there's much of a masqurade left with so many weird people, in full Krewe colours, too drunk and high to think about secrecy. Most people shut their doors, close the blinds and cower, but the street gangs are becoming reflections of Sin-Eater culture. And it's working, something about a dying city is letting them draw real power from those faux-occult gang signs every group is adopting.<br /> <br /> [edit] So long as I'm on the subject of the Ascending One's playing politics.<br /> <br /> 173: The Arab Spring, secular dictators falling and religious groups in to clean up the rubble. Who'd benefit from that? Mummies that's who. The Ascending One knows how to fight the Arisen, and they know why it's usually not worth their time. They've been pulling out of the Middle East, fortresses temples, drug warehouses. Move that shit somewhere safer like Africa. But they're not abandoning their duties, just adjusting their strategies. They're leaving behind cells of the best, hassassins. The high priests, the politicians the mummies put up, the cultists with the highest follower counts on twitter, if they can kill them fast enough the opportunity will fade away and Islamists rather than Iremites will end up in power.<br /> <br /> (Basically, the Arab Spring looks like it did in real life, because the Ascending Ones kept assassinating all the cultists trying to bring back Iremite theocracy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-01-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:54:26-08:00","id":331452,"title":"","content":"174: It's getting worse. The monsters were bad before, but ever since a few months ago, things have been bad. You though the monsters before bent the laws of nature; these things break it in ways that shred your sanity. It all started on the first night of the crescent moon, with the vanishing of a cell focused on studying witches, who called themselves &quot;The Promethean Brotherhood&quot;. Then it gets worse. You finally get to kill one of these things... And it turns into one of the missing Hunters, who manages to tell you a few words before dying: &quot;Rite... Trap... The Gate..&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T11:32:57-08:00","id":379243,"title":"","content":"175:<br /> <br /> <b>The Myth</b>: Slender Man<br /> <br /> <i>The Truth</i>: The Slender Man isn't a spirit, or one of the Others. Slender Man is a phenomena. A demonic influence that spreads from person to person and gains power from delusions and terror. He is a nightmare given life by people. He spreads like a virulent infection, using his self-inflicted victims as proxies. His story can be snuffed out, but he cannot die. Even if you run, even if his manifestation vanishes, you can escape from him no more than you can escape your own thoughts. He ends where memory does - hidden over time and sleeping like an old tale. He doesn't need to chase you. His shadow becomes real the moment you believe it. But Slender Man had to begin somewhere. And somewhere, there must be a way to stop him for good.<br /> <br /> <u>The Premise</u>: Your friend or someone important in your community is gone. Vanished into thin air after months of acting strangely. Tracking them down reveals them as a victim of something far more macabre than it might seem at first glance. The last in a trail of deadly incidents and disappearances that has spanned generations. If you follow, you must do so through hazy details, questionable accounts, and strange clues. And be prepared, let you become the next link in a chain of madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T16:59:03-08:00","id":379640,"title":"","content":"176: There are stories like it all over the place - the witch, the serial killer, the creature that peers through the windows at night. They pop up every few years, and people go missing as the monster follows a kind of occult schedule before the creature disappears once again. This one is real. You have the journals and rusted weaponry from a previous generation of hunters to prove it. The monster will appear again soon, and your cell is ready to take it down for good.<br /> <br /> Slight wrinkle - It looks like there are two of them now. But the patterns don't match, and monsters don't leave fingerprints. Everyone knows the story, and it looks like someone decided to play copycat, hiding their misdeeds behind the story of an urban legend. Can you afford to split your attention between a murderer and a monster before they both finish and disappear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T20:08:59-08:00","id":379773,"title":"","content":"<b>177: (Tier 1)</b> You're just coming home from a successful hunt when someone walks up to you and hands you an envelope.<br /> <br /> Apparently, they've been watching you for a while, and are looking to recruit... Do you trust them, or try to turn down their generous offer? After all, who <i>knows</i> how they'll respond to <i>that</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:28:41-08:00","id":397826,"title":"","content":"178: Your Cell's last hunt ended when the monster(s) you were pursuing managed to kill themselves in a large traffic pileup, Was the crash just an accident? if not who caused it, another cell, the monster(s) pulling a disappearing act, or something more sinister?...Have fun with the thorough investigation into this serious incident by the authorities as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T13:51:31-07:00","id":914348,"title":"","content":"179) Most Hunters don't have a long life expectancy, but this one has somehow managed to make it. They're a veteran of dozens of conflicts, and has managed to survive long enough to rack up an impressive collection of scars. A pillar of the local Vigil, they've likely helped out and been helped out by the players a couple of times, and now they've finally decided the pc Cell is trustworthy. They offer the players a way to really step up their game, to really take the fight to the monsters. If they agree, the veteran will introduce the players to their friend.<br /> <br /> And by &quot;friend&quot;, I mean the Hunter-Ghoul's <b>Domitor</b>.<br /> <br /> But don't worry, they insist. Their vampire is one of the <i>good ones</i>, and just wants to help. All they need to do is drink deep, and they'll have the power to light the night. Is the veteran somehow telling the truth, or are they just blinded by Vitae? Will the players turn on their former ally, and will anyone believe them if they tell the truth? Or will they chose to fall a little deeper into the darkness if it keeps the shadows at bay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:48:44-07:00","id":914494,"title":"","content":"180) Your cell's been gathering intel on this vampire for weeks now, but on a stakeout (ha!) of his haven, one of your team spots an unmarked van pull up out front, throw open the doors, and let loose a hunting pack of naked, pale /things/ that effortlessly found the bloodsucker and drained him dry. Similar reports pop up across town in the days that follow, painting a grim picture: someone - the government, maybe, or a big corporation - has things that crave vampires like they crave us.<br /> <br /> 181) An office worker casually smashes the glass case for the fire axe and cleaves a bloody swathe through his coworkers, but has no memory of the incident when the police finally stop his rampage. It's easy to write this off as an isolated incident of someone going postal... but it happens four more times in the same month, each time a normal, sane person lapsing into a fugue and swinging wildly with a hammer of hatchet. The media is spinning it as a violent mass hysteria, but the vigilant recognize it for what it is: possession by the spirit of a long-dead berserker. What brought this dead raider back to life? How can he be stopped? <br /> <br /> And perhaps most importantly: why is he so far from home?<br /> <br /> 182) (Utopia Now): Stupid people think you're just one of the dozens of tech startups trying to become the next industry giant, but you know you're building the future - and you've done terrible things to make that happen. So when a Chinese billionaire offers to buy out the entire organization, it understandably sets off alarm bells. He seems to have more money than God himself, and it looks like he didn't exist before last week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-14-2016, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T14:19:33-07:00","id":916421,"title":"","content":"183. The word comes down: The vampire club burns tonight. Several allied and trusted cells are coming with your own to help, until when you start tossing firebombs. Vampires, werewolves, witches, even revenants and fairies. The survivors fall back to the subway and quickly regroup. For now, the new goal is to survive and reach the Inquisition's church. Survive the night, and live to fight another day.<br /> <br /> &quot;Huuuunnnnnnters, come out to plaaaa-aaaay!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:27:00-07:00","id":918071,"title":"","content":"184) Old computers. Everybody has them, especially corporations, universities, and government bureaucracies. Mostly these dusty throwbacks take up room in forgotten closets, unable to be thrown away or recycled due to regulatory tangles and institutional recalcitrance. Recently though there's been a hot new start up actually <i>buying</i> this junk. The amount they pay isn't enough to raise suspicion, but its enough that most places don't say no. Ostensibly its all part of some green initiative or tech transfer to the developing world, but there have been some odd occurrences around them. What's their real end game, and what connection do they have to something called &quot;The Cryptovore&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:12:02-07:00","id":918099,"title":"","content":"185. Deep beneath the city are a system of catacombs so old their purpose has long been forgotten. In these dark tunnels dwell strange, sinewy, pale creatures that can see and somehow survive in this dank environment. This would be horrible enough alone, but things get much, much worse. These things are so inbred they cannot reproduce without human breeding stock. A cult of the wealthy elite in the city provides them just such, for a sinister purpose. You see, every now and then, a child born from these unwholesome unions is indistinguishable from a normal person, which a strange golden caul covering its eyes. In fact, they are always beautiful, charismatic, and incredibly lucky. The cult snatches these children up, adopt them into their families, and use the talents of the child as they grow up to ensure their continuing wealth and power. How will your cell deal with the horrors in the catacombs below, and can they escape the conspiracy in the city that works to protect these vile acts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T12:26:02-07:00","id":918179,"title":"","content":"186: The latest news is actually pretty good. The leeches aren't going out and biting unwilling necks, werewolves are keeping to cease fire lines, and witches just want to study their magic.<br /> <br /> So, of course, something goes wrong. Some dumbass mad scientist rolled into town with a small army of lackies, shouting from the hilltops that he wants all to bow to his will or die. To prove his point, he livestreamed the transformation of the city's oldest vampire from a withered husk of a man into a small rabbit. Which was then fed to the ghouls he turned into dogs.<br /> <br /> The important discovery is that this madman's creations can't even be touched by actual scientists who can explain why such creations can't work. So that's where your cell of rationalist Null Mysteriis members come in. Unfortunately, one group will fight tooth and nail to stop you; the Open-Minds the next town over who want to tout the &quot;genius&quot; as proof of their beliefs. Time to throw some science in this bitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T21:48:03-07:00","id":918436,"title":"","content":"187: Hunting for sport is already controversial among humane society groups, but even fellow hunters frown when someone kills an animal just for the fun of it. Recently, there have been reports of murders happening in the area. But the strange thing about the killings is that the victim is just left there for anybody to find. Nothing is stolen or planted on their body, there is no sign of a trophy being taken, no hidden clues or cryptic messages to decipher. Whoever the culprit is, they're killing people just because they have the power to do so, without any sign of a motive involved! It's up to your cell to put a stop to this bloodshed, and discover if it is supernatural in origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-21-2016, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T05:23:22-07:00","id":918566,"title":"","content":"188: The area Long Night cell is getting antsy. They keep screaming about signs of the end of the world in the morning coffee and of the Whore of Babylon like she's just moved in next door. Trying to calm them down only keeps them from getting crazier for about half a day before they go off on another tear of panic. You've tried hard to ignore them, but you're ready to start cracking skulls if they do something stupid one more time. Well, they did. They set up a bomb that would've killed the mayor, screaming about how he's one of the Devil's minions because the city tried to raise the property tax by .5%. No one likes paying taxes, but they like bombs in their city even less. Convince the bigger players in the local vigil that the Long Night cell has to go.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:12:54-07:00","id":918736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=918566#post918566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">188: The area Long Night cell is getting antsy. They keep screaming about signs of the end of the world in the morning coffee and of the Whore of Babylon like she's just moved in next door. Trying to calm them down only keeps them from getting crazier for about half a day before they go off on another tear of panic. You've tried hard to ignore them, but you're ready to start cracking skulls if they do something stupid one more time. Well, they did. They set up a bomb that would've killed the mayor, screaming about how he's one of the Devil's minions because the city tried to raise the property tax by .5%. No one likes paying taxes, but they like bombs in their city even less. Convince the bigger players in the local vigil that the Long Night cell has to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively: They're right, the apocalypse is just coming, the Whore of Babylon really is the next door neighbor of the Cell leader, the signs were indeed in the morning coffe(Just not all in one mug and you foolishly drank yours which was pretty important), the Mayor is member of a Demon cult that actually tries to avert whatever's going on, and the GM's getting even more crazy than usually, and you'll have to deal with it beacause you have managed to discredit the Long Night and all other hunters around are thinking of you as even more insane than them when you start saying they were right all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:22:21-07:00","id":918741,"title":"","content":"189) Back in the 80's there was a rumor about a mysterious arcade game called PRIMODE. Some kind of trippy puzzle game that was supposed to expand your brain but ended up giving people psych problems. People said all sorts of weird things about it: that it was a secret government project, that it was designed by a psychic wizard, that it was programmed using geometry from a dying star. You didn't think much about it until the disappearances started happening. People just walking outside and not coming back, leaving behind surreal drawings hidden in their abandoned belongings. Then you heard it on the radio, a short story tucked between bigger news, about a star NASA had been watching for the last couple decades that just exploded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:05:54-07:00","id":920346,"title":"","content":"190) Cheiron Group hunters have been turning up dead. Making it more disturbing is that some of their Thaumatech implants have been gruesomely removed. Your cell is racing against the clock to find the killer before the next hunter dies, knowing that any of you could be next. Imagine your horror to discover that all the missing implants seem to have come from the same &quot;donor&quot;, and that rather than being removed <i>they've been tearing their way out.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T15:47:09-07:00","id":920601,"title":"","content":"191: Britain is in an uproar. No, not over Brexit, the hunters are calling to the world for help. It seems that an order of knights swearing allegiance to the court of Arthur has started attacking hunter cells, ordering hunters to swear magically enforced oaths of loyalty. They claim that Arthur will soon return from Avalon, and reforge England in its darkest hour.<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe it does have to do with Brexit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T17:32:54-07:00","id":920648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=920601#post920601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">191: Britain is in an uproar. No, not over Brexit, the hunters are calling to the world for help. It seems that an order of knights swearing allegiance to the court of Arthur has started attacking hunter cells, ordering hunters to swear magically enforced oaths of loyalty. They claim that Arthur will soon return from Avalon, and reforge England in its darkest hour.<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe it does have to do with Brexit.</div> </div> </div> </div>192.) making the situation even weirder, is the involvement of a clan of werewolves claiming to be descendants of Sir Marrok, the round table's resident werewolf and, according to the legends King Arthur's chief bodyguard. While they are known to be helping the aforementioned knights, their main concern appears to be causing trouble for the werewolf leaders of ireland and scotland, who reluctantly swore vassalage to the Marroks when their homelands became part of the UK, so that they don't use Brexit as justification to rebel against them. The resulting werewolf civil war has led to hunter cells being used as deniable assets by the various werewolf factions, who pay them in money and stranger things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T19:14:29-07:00","id":920717,"title":"","content":"<b>193:</b> A political candidate, one most of your cell doesn't like, is coming to town on the campaign trail. What's more, when they've arrived, they've sought the cell out. They've been vouched for and sent to you by a trusted ally, and was apparently a fairly prolific hunter before an encounter with a particular evil that left only the candidate alive and able to continue the vigil. They have it from their own trusted sources that a particularly nasty group of baddies is going to be rising up in your town, soon, and they want to your help to stop it before it gets out of control.<br /> <br /> Can the cell put aside their differences and work with this old hand? Will you put down a force of evil that threatens your very homes? Or is it a trick?<br /> <br /> Apologies for the lengths of these but figured it needed some setting.<br /> <br /> <b>194:</b> Nice, wholesome town in the middle of nowhere. Not even old-fashioned, some of the people are pretty modern and almost everyone is open minded and accepting. The place seems blessed. Cancer rates are at a flat zero, as are many other diseases, the old seem to live well past the national average, every citizen's business is a success, farms are lush and abundant and haven't needed any outside help. Children are born healthy and hale, those who go off to war come back with in one piece. Other, more predatory supernaturals seem to avoid the place, not out of any fear, they're just subtly guided away.<br /> <br /> Of course, as every hunter knows, one thing good in life is too good to be true. And they're right. Four sacrifices a year. They believe they're good people, it's worth it. They try to use criminals, but the crime rate is so low as it is. A lot of people pass through, perhaps intrigued by some 'Mom and Pop' store or another, or seduced by a particularly striking citizen. Better an outsider than one of your friends, or relatives, right? That's what they decide, anyways.<br /> <br /> The sacrifice isn't to any monster. It's a rite, and only works within the city limits, and the heads of every household know how to perform it, having watched and assisted in it over the years.<br /> <br /> Maybe they're just passing through. Maybe they were born there. Maybe a friend has gone missing and you're sure they were there, and you know these people are lying when they say they don't know your buddy. What, if anything, is to be done?<br /> <br /> <b>195:</b> Because some people give the benefit of the doubt to small towns, or might not see harm in it. Same town, same situation, but with a new conflict.<br /> <br /> Someone else has found out about the rite, and not an individual but an Organization. Maybe it's Cheiron, finding that their implants are wild successes when performed in the limits. Maybe it's some mad scientist of a Centimani, who finds that they form no Wasteland as long as they stay, maybe something more sinister. Or something entirely mundane, like a 'normal' cult who finds their practices and preaching just work better there, or a company whose products made in town just sell better, dominating the market, the training facility they've built churning out money-making super-executives, loyal to the corp.<br /> <br /> And they're taking over. They've influenced elections, bought out mortgages, have had people driven out of town and sometimes just disappeared. Their people are in the positions of power, and they're not going to stop until there's no competition. A town that had maybe four accidental deaths a year has shot up to twenty. They want to benefit from the rite, no one else.<br /> <br /> <b>196</b>: Every Friday night at 11:15, there's a Breaking News announcement, and reporter Melissa Mendez informs you of a crime that, to you, was obviously committed by a supernatural. Often one you never would have found yourself. The problem is, Miss Mendez has been dead for years. A member of Network Zero, she was killed while trying to let everyone know what was going on. Her spirit lives on, pointing you in the direction of danger through her news alerts.<br /> <br /> The problem is, she doesn't stop. If you ignore her message, 15 past the hour, every hour, it keeps popping up on any tv you can perceive. Even if it's off or unplugged, the device manages to activate to urge you to do something about it. If you've decided to get rid of your tv the message finds its way into computer banner ads and in every car radio within earshot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-25-2016, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:19:35-07:00","id":921544,"title":"","content":"197: To the untrained eye, it looks like any other vase from the early Classic period of Greece, specifically from the area around Athens. As a member of the Spear and Shield, you know it as the ancient legendary item Pandora's Box. It's empty of course, but one day a man comes to you with an offer. Claiming to be the big Z himself, he offers to guide your cell to hunt down all of mankind's ills in exchange for the honor of being elevated to the level of a demigod. To prove his credentials, he calls down Heracles and Hera in the middle of another &quot;You're not my real mother&quot; spat.<br /> <br /> Okay, the Greek gods want you to hunt down the residents of Pandora's Box. Nothing suspicious about this at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T20:11:14-07:00","id":921827,"title":"","content":"198) There's a rumor going around Task Force: VALKYRIE. A lot of resources in FORT are being diverted toward a special project with very high clearance, ADAMSKI has been covering up bizarre goings on in a block of warehouses, TAKOMA has been receiving strange work orders even by their standards, and TWILIGHT has been processing an unusually large number of new confidential informants in the &quot;Changeling&quot; community. Something big is in the works, something you've heard called MORDRED. It looks like they might be doing recon in an interstitial realm with the help of knowledgeable guides, but you're starting to suspect that's just the beginning. When the file crossed your desk connecting dozens of missing persons to an ENE involved in cross-dimensional human trafficking the whole thing fell into place. They're planning a raid on the other side, deeper than anyone has ever gone and come out again, with a vanguard of vengeful Changelings outfitted with Task Force weaponry and training. They're going to exfiltrate one of the Others.<br /> <br /> God help them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:29:33-07:00","id":922278,"title":"","content":"199: UFO sightings and spacemen are bubkiss, it's the oceans that have the really freaky stuff. Sea monsters, immortal giant crabs, merpeople, and...Catholics?! That's right, somehow a clan of fish-people were converted when the Church was in it's infancy, and they want to rebuild their own way of worship with Rome. So now you have to handle whatever fallout occurs.<br /> - Malleus Maleficarum: Worse, you have to deal with ministering to them. Two millennia of isolation have bred a vastly different interpretation of Christ's teachings utterly at odds with current canon law. So good luck telling the fish-people that they didn't need to kill and eat one of their own every Friday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:54:03-07:00","id":922696,"title":"","content":"200. When Devora gave birth to her child, she expected a pretty little girl that should could dress up like her favorite porcelain dolls and brush her hair all nice and straight. Instead, her daughter Evelyn was born with a bright red birthmark on her face, and frizzy hair like her father's. Devora was mortified, but soon devised a way to realize her dream. She fashioned a porcelain mask, and a lovely straight wig, and forced Evelyn to wear it around the house. She put her in child-sized doll clothing, and even locked her in a velvet lined truck at night. One day, when Devora's husband could take no more, he tried to leave and take little Evelyn with him. There was a struggle, and when the two crashed into a table with lit candles on it, the old house went up in flames. Little Evelyn was still locked in her trunk in the attic, and no one ever found her. It has been twenty years since that night, and somehow, Evelyn has returned. Donning the cracked and charred mask her mother made for her years ago, she now prowls the streets at night, finding the &quot;pretty children&quot; and murdering them with a pair of her mother's fabric shears. She will prove to her mother once and for all that she is a pretty girl, even if it means killing all the others. Can your cell put this broken dolly back in her box, for good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:06:12-07:00","id":922834,"title":"","content":"<b>201:</b> Cults are always bad news, right? When they are not making gruesome sacrifices to edlritch beings, they are leeching from their members down to the last drop and destroying lives. And they're never open about their practices, which only makes the situation worse. Imagine the Cell's surprise when they receive mail inviting them to a new religion whose members are dedicated to tracking down and neutralizing the dangerous parts of <b>other </b>cults. They even have a website, with a list of benefits for joining and contributing.<br /> <br /> It seems they have found a way to reverse-engineer the tainted Essence and other supernatural energies that center on cursed artifacts, the body parts of malevolent entities and so on. They harness it into a physical compound that is not unlike the Tass that some Mages use, and they're looking for help on how to market and mass produce it. The compound makes one a lot more resistant to influence from malignant ephemerals, especially mind control and bodily transformation.<br /> <br /> The Cell stands to gain a lot of money and free samples, but what about the possible side effects? They don't seem to be affiliated with Cheiron, and their leader is a charismatic and inventive sort who likes to meet in person and freely shares the Cult's knowledge. He insists that mankind is capable of cleaning the world of any entities that feed on our vices and make everything worse, but he is oddly scientific about this mission. Is he onto something? He says he's done some self-experimentation on his free time, and the results are impressive to say the least...<br /> <br /> Inspired by the discussion thread for Deviant. The cult's leader is doing research on cures for the negative effects of powers like Fetter and Claiming, and how to artificially reproduce the positive parts with no ephemerals involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-28-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T17:16:57-07:00","id":923580,"title":"","content":"202: Stephen King should never direct coked out of his skull, because he might just be right about a few things. A group of vehicles of various makes and models have come alive, but aren't immediately hostile due to their owners care and maintenance. They want to communicate, to learn about emotions and what it means to be sapient. Think you're up for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 09-11-2020, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T14:32:19-07:00","id":929389,"title":"","content":"203: (TFV) They finally did it. Scifi authors have been predicting that combat-capable mechs are imminent since Wells' Martian tripods, but aside from a few weird things you've heard rumors about, and the odd wonky prototype, no government has officially put anything like it into development. But word is that Project Euparkeria is the real deal, a bipedal armored vehicle capable of surprising speed and agility. The walker's designers have scheduled a product demonstration to show off what it can do, and security is high. But it isn't just the usual- your cell has been called on to monitor the demonstration with some vague militarese about &quot;your unique skillsets may be required&quot;. That's pretty much a dead giveaway that some supernatural force has shown interest in this new weapon...or in the all star selection of top military personnel who will be attending the event. <br /> <br /> 204: Mass sightings of a particular type of being or phenomena are always bad news, but these are even stranger than normal. Instead of mass reports of bodies drained of blood or giant hairy beasts or UFOs, you've started hearing about mysterious people showing up all over the globe, claiming to be citizens of countries that don't exist and carrying IDs, passports, and credit cards that don't correspond to any known nation or bank. Not only that, these mysterious castaways seem to be from the same alternate universe, since they seem to understand each other perfectly. This is going to be a pain to cover up...and an absolute nightmare to understand. <br /> <br /> 205: There's something haunting your town or city, stalking the back alleys and picking off prey with supernatural skill. Only thing is, this entity looks almost like a caricature of a hunter- witnesses say it wears a long coat and a bulletproof vest, and it usually brandishes a stake, fire axe, or shotgun. It can pass for human, but those who have seen it up close say it looks almost like a heavily stylized drawing, with impossibly long leanly muscled limbs and a face more grim and determined than a stone carving of a puritan witch hunter. All of its victims have had some connection to the supernatural, as well. How do you handle an entity that seems to be doing your job for you? How about when the local supernatural communities start to wonder if you somehow summoned this creature?<br /> <br /> 206: Few Hunters aren't plagued by some degree of financial woes, so the offer that arrived is pretty tempting. One of those fantastically rich eccentric billionaires has somehow tracked down your cell and is impressed with your track record, so he's willing to pay a ton to hire you on as security. See, he's recently purchased a relic rumored to have incredible supernatural power, and he's planning on moving it from its secret location to a specially prepared vault. He wants you to provide an escort for it, because he's sure that certain parties are going to want to get their hands on it, and once he removes it from its resting place, any being with magical senses will be able to detect the power it radiates. <br /> <br /> 207: Ashwood Abbey is prepping for one of its biggest events ever. They've used their connections to get Central Park completely to themselves for the night, and they've brought in some &quot;experts&quot; to set up powerful wards around the park. Their plan is to release a bunch of dangerous cryptids and creatures inside the park, and have a grand old time hunting them. That would be bad enough, but what happens when the various transports bringing the creatures into the city are all hit and wrecked simultaneously, unleashing the creatures into the city itself?<br /> <br /> 208: (TFV/ADAMSKI) There's a hot new big budget paranormal reality show getting ready to premiere, so that means it's time to do what ADAMSKI does best: misdirect. The Men in Black have a simple task: turn the show into a laughingstock before it accidentally stumbles onto anything genuine. Unfortunately, the True Believer in the starring role is unusually dedicated and perceptive, and he starts to suspect that the &quot;experts&quot; and &quot;witnesses&quot; have been planted to discredit him. If he could somehow find proof of this, TFV is looking at a crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-10-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:12:32-07:00","id":929438,"title":"","content":"208: Racing, it's a sport no matter how you slice it. New age coliseums where nomex-clad gladiators race each other and luck itself to win the big prize. Your cell just lives near one of the smaller racetracks, so you don't usually give it too much notice. Only today, there's been a strange find at the track. Someone found what looks like a burned tire in the middle of pit row, a number painted in the center of it. The organizers treat it as a prank, until that same car winds up crashed into the wall. The driver survived, but the car is toast and the team out for the season. The organizers think it's mundane sabotage of some kind, but you have to be suspicious. Was it just mundane sabotage dressed up as a ritual, or are more drivers about to risk their necks?<br /> <br /> 209 (TFV): Parris Island has been hit. Marine contacts have been reporting recruits just waking up and walking right into the jaws of the alligators in the swamps surrounding the island. Officially, it's all being written off as the stress of training the best America has to offer with the pledge that the Marine Corps will &quot;modify&quot; its standards to prevent further incidents. The evidence says otherwise, as drill instructors are unable to restrain the Marines they do find literally marching to their dooms. The records state that these were the standout recruits, the ones with bright futures in the Corps right ahead of them. Further, the records report that one Marine in the 1950s did march right to the gators. Any other cell would assume it's the vengeful ghost of that lost recruit, but you're paid too much to assume. Something is using the incident as a cover, find what really wants to kill these future Marines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T20:48:21-08:00","id":1015517,"title":"","content":"210: Living quietly in the city, there is a woman who is a textbook monster in every way but behavior - she keeps to herself, doesn't harm humans, and her live has been shaped by the effort of appearing outwardly normal in order to have something like a normal life. Having been this way for as long as she can remember, her existence has somehow been been revealed to the local hunters and she is in particular danger from-<br /> <br /> - The malleus malificarum, long night and even lucifuge, being a succubus. With stubby horns, the classic spade-tipped tail and an impossibly beautiful body, she can only really go out during Halloween and must work from home. Blessed items react to her as if she was a true demon, though she is entirely flesh-and-blood, binding or banishing rituals do nothing to her. Is this a curse or a demon in denial?<br /> <br /> - The union, after the lake she lives next to suffers a rash of drownings, mainly male children. The Rusalka swears she is not responsible for their deaths, and even has an alibi in a few cases, but who knows what the supernatural are capable of? She begs the cell to clear her name before hunters come after her with fire, guns, and 'how to kill a river spirit' they got off google translate. Did someone get their mythology wrong, or is this just a very canny murderess?<br /> <br /> - Null mysteriis and TASKFORCE: valkryie. Bad sci-fi movies aside, this robot girl is more interested in living her life than trying to kill all meatbags. Her creator/father passed away years ago, and an internet connection is all she needs to explore the world. She's a miracle of science, seemingly made without any supernatural assistance, and that makes her very valuable to the kind of people who believe in human rights for humans alone - taking her apart would advance science by decades. If her arguments about the nature of life and consciousness can't sway you, then consider what a group of amoral scientists could do with an army of killer robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:32:57-07:00","id":1115807,"title":"","content":"<b><i><u>LIVE!!!</u></i></b><br /> <br /> 211: Did you hear about what's been going on in Nebraska? The story is that someone has held up a convenience store run by a werewolf, and things got ugly. From there a werewolf holy war has seemingly been launched, groups of werewolves grabbing hunter families and using them as ritual sacrifices in sick ceremonies. The only way to stop this might be investigating the source, and that means traveling deep into enemy territory.<br /> <br /> 212: A satellite is said to have orbited the Earth since before men made it into space. Called &quot;The Black Knight&quot;, the satellite is anything from an observer of humankind to a doomsday weapon. The only way to know for sure is to investigate. One of the conspiracies has ponied up the money, but can't afford to lose their best to something that might not even be their kind of problem. So congratulations, you're going to be the first hunter in space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T10:05:18-07:00","id":1116877,"title":"","content":"213: Old Ben Jackson, he's a fixture in the hunter community. He was the man that finally exorcised the Young property, and was the lynchpin figure when the area cells decided that the witches were a problem too big to ignore. He just sent out a message; terminal cancer from his years of work in the plant. His last request? Kill the vampire lord that he never could, and get his entire personal archive.<br /> <br /> 214: (Ashwood Abbey) It was a good idea for a Halloween treat, hold a seance at the &quot;good&quot; Rev. Ogilvy's grave. Only the dear reverend has been away from the pleasures of the flesh for far too long, and has possessed one of your number, the local barrister. The man has a public reputation for being tough yet fair at the bench, as well as being a devoted father and husband involved in dozens of charity projects. If Ogilvy goes too wild, it threatens to drag the entire Abbey into the open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T14:07:14-07:00","id":1116972,"title":"","content":"215) It's always tragic when a soldier can no longer imagine returning to civilian life. Recently, your city has been on the verge of being 100% supernatural free; the goal of every respectable Hunter for as long as anybody can remember. But despite victory being within their grasp, one particular cell has other plans. Their leader has become addicted to the war against the supernatural. Having a license to kill and an enemy that has no legal rights makes them feel empowered. So, while all the other hunters are distracted finishing off the last few stragglers, they concoct a plan to renew the war in earnest. They're going to unleash a wave of monsters upon the city so they can keep doing what they love; killing without consequences!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T16:01:46-07:00","id":1117978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=1116972#post1116972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">215) It's always tragic when a soldier can no longer imagine returning to civilian life. Recently, your city has been on the verge of being 100% supernatural free; the goal of every respectable Hunter for as long as anybody can remember. But despite victory being within their grasp, one particular cell has other plans. Their leader has become addicted to the war against the supernatural. Having a license to kill and an enemy that has no legal rights makes them feel empowered. So, while all the other hunters are distracted finishing off the last few stragglers, they concoct a plan to renew the war in earnest. They're going to unleash a wave of monsters upon the city so they can keep doing what they love; killing without consequences!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 216) But what if he knows something you don't? What if you haven't freed your city from the supernatural, but only snipped off the most visible buds? What if your enemy cell is just trying to bring the supernatural ecosystem back into balance? <br /> <br /> Choose wisely, choose logically, but most of all, choose quickly...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:45:43-07:00","id":1122413,"title":"","content":"217: A local cell of leading hunters are in disagreement. A third of the group wants to focus solely on combating the monsters, a third are more focused on trying to understand them, and a third want to develop better means of understanding the occult. No one wants this cell to break up, they're too valuable to the local Vigil. They want a third party to come in to give them an outside opinion on what the better option is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T12:06:49-08:00","id":1191068,"title":"","content":"[Lights another candle for the thread]<br /> <br /> <b>218)</b> One of your contacts has occasional, random prophetic abilities. Just yesterday, they sent your Cell a warning to &quot;beware the Ides of March&quot;.<br /> <b>a)</b> As the day draws closer, you've been noticing the silhouettes of owls perched on the branches outside your home. Leech activity in the area has dropped too. Wonder why.<br /> <b>b)</b> The message also said something about spiders and tangled webs. Your Cell-mate has become worried that it might be a reference to their new girlfriend, who they say has been acting more agitated recently and also <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1188594-and-a-trophy-made-from-my-enemies?p=1190034#post1190034\">hates spiders</a>.<br /> <b>c)</b> You Cell starts tracking down leads to a big-time monster you've been pursuing. On the 14th, you've managed to chase it into a crossroads and lose track of which way it went. In the distance, you can see <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Watchtower\" target=\"_blank\">5 towers</a>, and each of your is arguing over which way it must have went.<br /> <br /> <b>219)</b> Your Cell has accomplished much in the 5 years you've been together. Now an ally has asked you to perform a task they were never able to - rescuing their sister from some monstrous abductor that stole them away 5 years ago. Doing so will mean going into some kind of other-realm called &quot;the Hedge&quot;, finding the trail, and stealing the sister back.<br /> <br /> It was tough, but you've managed to find her. Unfortunately, you've also found doppelgangers of <i>yourselves</i> who claim they are you, taken away along with her, a few days ago. They <i>have</i> to be lying, but how do they know so much about your life prior to then?<br /> <br /> <b>220)</b> One of your Cell (or an important Contact or Ally) has always been a tech-head. Well, they've just gotten the latest smart phone that is supposed to come equipped with a rudimentary Artificial Intelligence. It doesn't sound as mechanical and pre-recorded as other virtual assistants, sure, but AI? That's fiction. Except... this keeps using turns of phrase and reminding you of things <i>just like</i> a friend you lost contact with. Last you heard, they were going to work with some new tech company. Actually, it looks like the same one behind the phone (through a shell corporation)... <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1183958-ghosts-in-the-machine-brain-uploading-and-seed-ai?p=1184207#post1184207\">Elysium Concepts Limited</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-03-2018, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T03:58:24-07:00","id":1194785,"title":"","content":"<b>221)</b> Your Cell was having a normal meeting, until the lights went out and you were all knocked unconscious by waves of men in dark suits.<br /> <br /> Next thing you know, you come to in a dark room with a single light illuminating a terminal. Surrounded by monsters. Who say they are your <i>Cell-mates</i>. When you check, <i>you</i> are a monster too.<br /> <br /> Then you are given your &quot;mission&quot; - use your knowledge of the area's supernatural factions to infiltrate the monsters' organizations and eliminate a threat. Do this, and you can go back to the way you were. But the clock is ticking.<br /> <br /> <b>a)</b> The organization is an up-and-coming Conspiracy, that is trying out their experimental techno-occult mutagen on your Cell. Use the forms of monsters to join and destroy their societies, and the Vigil might have a new weapon in its arsenal. Don't worry, they promise to give you the anti-mutagen once the mission is successful. Provided you can take it in time, there should be no long-term consequences.<br /> <br /> <b>b)</b> The group responsible is another Cell - turns out a group of monsters were going to usurp your bodies to destroy the local Hunter community from the inside. The other Cell was able to decipher a ritual that would, in a twist of poetic justice, turn the monsters' own trick back upon them. The other Cell is working on how to get you back to your own bodies... before your minds fade into oblivion and the monsters' wills return.<br /> <br /> <b>c)</b> A Conspiracy calling itself CONTROL has been in the practice of implanting/infecting monsters with a kind of techno-occult Malware. They capture a target, perform The Procedure upon them, and can then know what it knows, and even influence their behavior. Even control them via remote piloting. CONTROL has conscripted you as &quot;emergency assets&quot; to deal with a critical matter using your exclusive experience. They have &quot;activated&quot; some of their &quot;Supernatural Resources&quot; in the region and put you in control - complete the objectives while control persists and they will let you go, or even extend an offer.<br /> <br /> [This is designed for giving Hunters a taste at playing Monsters, Dread Powers and all.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T08:59:08-07:00","id":1194857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=1194785#post1194785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> snip</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Side effects may include hallucinations, suicidal thoughts or actions, high blood pressure, <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">rapid onset of existential crisis, </span></span></span>and a persistent hunger for human flesh. Please speak to your doctor immediately, as these could become permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T16:39:18-07:00","id":1207446,"title":"","content":"<b>222)</b> Your Cell has recently been attacked by another Cell accusing you of being &quot;Cancerous&quot;. According to them, you are all in bed with the monsters. Literally. They think all of your groups' Significant (or merely recent) Others are monsters. How are you going to get them off your back? You <i>couldn't</i> have been so fooled. Could you? What will it mean if the accusations are true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T09:07:59-07:00","id":1234024,"title":"","content":"223). Surprise of all surprises, but a local Mask has started killing people in your area. He's even using a calling card, stuffing a Missing Person poster into the mouth of all of his victims. However, as the cell starts to take a closer look at the missing person it becomes clear that this girl is actually <i>related</i> to the Mask. Just what the hell is going on here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24370-mourge40k","name":"mourge40k","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T11:15:11-07:00","id":1235300,"title":"","content":"224. A sudden spike in the murder rate worries authorities and quickly the Player Characters quickly get roped into it. However all these murders couldn't have being done by one man and with a bit of investigation the PC's realize that there's a serial killer convention and they have decided to host in your city. Time to shut it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23615-pierrew","name":"Pierrew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T17:18:35-07:00","id":1256287,"title":"","content":"<b>225)</b> For nearly as long as you have been a Hunter, you've had a particular monster who has been your arch nemesis. You've been trying to kill each other for who knows how long, and yet you two always manage to survive and escape somehow. But that might be coming to an end, because today, you awoke to find yourself in a place that was not your own, in a body that was much the same. It would seem that you and your nemesis have exchanged bodies while your sleeping, and now you've become the very monster you have sworn to destroy.<br /> <br /> But that's not the worst of it, because once you take to the streets in search of answers, your former cell shows up, lead by the impostor, who, like always, seems especially keen on erasing you from this world!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T11:30:23-07:00","id":1256996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=264085#post264085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> meanwhile, the hunter PC's other kid gets beaten up at school by a pack of teenage werewolves who then use the PC's identity as a hunter to claim self defense in court... and it works</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>&quot;It took an entire pack of werewolves to beat up a single, unarmed, human child? Wow, and here I thought you guys had a code of honor!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-24-2018, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:39:56-07:00","id":1382612,"title":"","content":"226) A message just came down the line. There was a prototype-copy of the Lansing Facility built just outside a nearby town. It was occupied by something like 40 slashers (this number does not have to be accurate). It was just busted wide open by weird, anti-prison activists. You're being sent in to do whatever you can to clean this mess up. Good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:45:33-07:00","id":1382613,"title":"","content":"227) A gathering of hunters is been organized. It's being held in a big, fancy hotel. The kind you could only dream of getting a room at. You've gotten a invitation. It says &quot;you+1&quot;.<br /> When you get there you find hunters from practically every Compact &amp; Conspiracy in attendance. There's a couple of hunters from some &quot;Confederacies&quot;, whatever those are. Some of the hunters have used their +1 to bring a friendly supernatural with them. Some of the local supernaturals have crashed the gathering to see what's going on, &amp; to be annoying.<br /> So far all is good.<br /> Then, early the next morning there is a bone-chilling scream. A dead body has been found. In one of the hotel's rooms. All you know for certain is that it wasn't natural causes, that the victim had attended last night's gathering of hunters, &amp; that the police have already been called.<br /> \u2022 This hook has a lot of pieces. To make it easier I have come up with some ideas for characters to turn up in the story. You could also rummage through various sourcebooks &amp; threads to make up the numbers. Whatever works for you.<br /> <br /> Potential Attendees<br /> \u25cf A middle-ranked (not a foot soldier, not one of the heads) Invictus ventrue who's come to represent Invictus. He has no desire to rise beyond where he currently is, because there are peasants, there are lords, &amp; then there are those in between. I think he crashed the gathering.<br /> \u25cf A small pack of Uratha that work with TFV, fighting whatever threats may surface within their territory. Come in as the +1's for some TFV hunters.<br /> \u25cf An old willworker built like a brick shithouse. The mage has discovered that they are dying &amp; upon learning of tjis gathering, has decided to hand over his life's work to all the hunters that he can. His life's work being the accumulated knowledge of the Abyss &amp; it's &quot;servants/phenomena/etc.&quot; collected over nearly seventy years of combating it. Crashed the gathering.<br /> \u25cf Some Horrors &amp; Brief Nightmares.<br /> \u25cf A number of local supernaturals that have been sent in by their respective factions to represent.<br /> \u25cf A group of six so-called &quot;demigods&quot;. One Egyptian one. One Greek one. One Nordic one. One Mesoamerican one. One Yoruban/Voodoo one. One Japanese one. Not here to attend the gathering, just rooming in the same hotel.<br /> \u25cf Random people with minor supernatural templates &amp; Merits.<br /> \u25cf A shartha looking for a useful future vessel.<br /> <br /> Supplementary Events<br /> \u25cf One of the hotel rooms is haunted.<br /> \u25cf There are a group of dormant Pandorans in the basement. They wake up if a Promethean gets close enough.<br /> \u25cf There is a colony of goblin-roaches in the hotel gardens.<br /> \u25cf A local spirit noble calls upon some of the hunters to give a ruling at a courtroom trial for spirits. They have been selected for this task as the spirits are having trouble themselves &amp; the hunters are a neutral party.<br /> \u25cf Some of the people in the hotel are experiencing horrific nightmares. The nightmares appear to be of Begotten origin, but none of the Begotten that are here appear to be responsible.<br /> \u25cf Two werewolf packs are gearing up for a brawl in the middle of the hotel's foyer.<br /> \u25cf One vampire accuses another of messing with the memory of one of the attending hunter's.<br /> \u25cf A changeling accuses an attending hunter of being a copy of the changeling, &amp; a servant of the &quot;True Fae&quot;.<br /> \u25cf A Huntsman crashes the event to grab an attending changeling.<br /> \u25cf A willworker brought with them a mystical item that they made, to show it off.<br /> \u25cf A hunter becomes one of the Bound.<br /> <br /> Various Characters<br /> \u25cf Hotel Staff<br /> \u25cf Hotel Attendees<br /> \u25cf Local Cops<br /> \u25cf Hunters that got invites to the gathering<br /> \u25cf People that got brought along as &quot;+1's&quot;<br /> \u25cf Local members of the supernatural community that have decided (or been ordered to) to &quot;crash the party&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:47:13-07:00","id":1382614,"title":"","content":"228) You've come upon a slasher unlike any other. Seriously, this one is quite possibly a one-of-a-kind.<br /> This slasher exclusively targets other slashers. The only real problem with them is they get tunnel vision &amp; don't really care how bad any collateral damage is, as long as the opposing slashers die, permanently.<br /> Now, how do they unfailingly identify other slashers, hmm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:47:47-07:00","id":1382615,"title":"","content":"229) Something blatantly supernatural is recreating the plots of certain creepypastas/urban legends.<br /> The media is loving it &amp; is milking the shit out of the situation, but everyone even vaguely involved is feeling very uncomfortable about these events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:49:12-07:00","id":1382617,"title":"","content":"230) (Silver Cross, Skin &amp; Bones) You've decided to help out at the &quot;Silver Cross&quot; clinic your uncle volunteers at. He was vehemently opposed to this but you're not really sure why that was.<br /> First day on the job, everything's going good, no drama.<br /> Some guy just walked in with a weird wound on his arm. The guy's friends follow him inside. Apparently the &quot;wasp nest&quot; in his arm is damaged &amp; his usual doctor is unavailable. And then there's the person? whose tentacle is wounded.<br /> Your uncle's life is so much more interesting than you thought it was. How again did you get this job?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:51:15-07:00","id":1382618,"title":"","content":"231) (Chosen of Kroll, Skin &amp; Bones) Kroll is a good dude. It might have more in common with Cthulhu, Nyarlathotep, or Azathoth, but it's a good dude.<br /> It's also a god, of sorts, &amp; just as the God of Abraham had Jesus Christ, Kroll has it's own &quot;son&quot; now.<br /> The only real problem the Chosen can see here is that despite being such a good dude, Kroll is still an inhuman abomination that from well outside human reality. How the hell is Kroll's son gonna fit into the level of humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:52:05-07:00","id":1382619,"title":"","content":"232) You're a newly formed cell of hunters &amp; you've lucked out. You found someone (probably a supernatural someone but you're not caring) that has identified multiple supernatural individuals who should be removed from life/unlife.<br /> Time to go proactive!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:52:46-07:00","id":1382620,"title":"","content":"233) Dissecting a new monster for unusual thaumatech has resulted in a contagion of sorts.<br /> Those that catch it develop a high fever. Once the fever passes a power will develop (draw from Mage, Changeling, Vampire, Werewolf, Hunter, Demon, Princess, Leviathan, Siren, blue books, etc. for powers). These powers are unaffected by whatever it is that keeps the mundane populace from noticing them.<br /> Several of the newly empowered have gotten it into their heads to be superheroes/supervillains/etc. &amp; an organization has grown to take advantage of these empowered.<br /> Meanwhile, the Cheiron Group is scrambling to take back control of the situation, &amp; many other supernatural factions are looking smug about Cheiron's predicament whilst adjusting their own power bases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:53:40-07:00","id":1382621,"title":"","content":"234) A close friend, though one that doesn't hold the vigil, has been kidnapped by a vampire &amp; taken deep into the local Nosferatu Necropolis. How are you going to rescue them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:54:39-07:00","id":1382622,"title":"","content":"235) (TFV) A case has recently been relabeled to being a Black Book case. The case involves a creature that has been identified as the Narrow Man.<br /> The Narrow Man has no facial features to speak of. It is very skinny &amp; wears a fitted suit. It is extremely harmful towards anyone who notices it, alternating between mind control &amp; homicide. This might make some people decide that the best thing to do would be to just leave it alone, but the creature is a local urban legend &amp; many ghost hunters, teenagers, etc. have gone out looking for the bloody thing. Additionally, evidence suggests that the Narrow Man goes out of its way to get noticed, it might be that it literally cannot effect anyone until they notice it, at least directly.<br /> In spite of all this the primary reasons why this case has moved to the Black Book is that body of the Narrow Man can be killed, but then the &quot;spirit&quot; immediately takes over the nearby body of someone who has noticed it, warping the newly stolen body into a perfect replica of its own. We've already lost three(?) teams to this thing.<br /> PS: creature also appears to have spatial distortion capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:56:33-07:00","id":1382624,"title":"","content":"236) You've recently crossed three sister witches with very different powers.<br /> The eldest taps into the ephemeral currents of the world to mimic the powers of twilight beings.<br /> The second born rely's on the power of blood or Vitae to fuel her magic.<br /> The youngest steals her power more directly from the flesh &amp; blood of the animals (&amp; stranger things) she kills.<br /> You've taken on far more powerful foes so this should be a cakewalk, right? Well, it turns out no, these three sisters are doing you some serious damage.<br /> \u2022 Inspired by the CofD supplement &quot;Borrowed Power&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 01-28-2021, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:04:48-07:00","id":1383565,"title":"","content":"237) A month ago you were on a hunt that resembled Rumpelstiltskin. Last week you had a hunt that reminded you of Snow White. A couple of nights ago there was that was reminiscent of Hansel &amp; Gretel.<br /> Who or what is bringing forth fairytales to life in your neighbourhood &amp; how can you stop it?<br /> <br /> \u25cf These are not the modern-day, sanitized versions of the fairy tales that are being played out by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:07:18-07:00","id":1383566,"title":"","content":"238) Out of the blue you got attacked by a rather vicious werewolf.<br /> You manage to win the battle &amp; as you stand victorious over your dying foe they confess something rather troubling.<br /> Apparently they didn't want to attack you, but some external energy wormed its way inside &amp; forced the issue, targeting the werewolf like a gun in your direction.<br /> It seems that you have a hidden enemy, now who or what is it?<br /> \u25cf I see the hidden enemy as being a group of Lupus et Fidelis, but I feel it's vague enough to come up with your own hidden enemy if you want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:08:32-07:00","id":1383567,"title":"","content":"239) You've found your way to a stall in a goblin market.<br /> The stall is hiring out what sound like copies of various Endowments in exchange for memories, friendships, accomplishments, skills, &amp; etc. appropriate to whatever Endowment you're getting.<br /> What do want to hire/buy? And what are you willing to give up in exchange?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:09:44-07:00","id":1383568,"title":"","content":"240) People appear to have started committing suicide by jumping down from very high heights, very quickly.<br /> Then one of your friends becomes the latest victim of this phenomenon, so you decide to investigate.<br /> You discover a group of shapeshifting falcon people. The skydiving situation is a part of their recruitment &amp; the those that hit the ground have failed the test.<br /> Okay, that's understandable. Not forgivable, but understandable. Now why are they doing so much recruitment?<br /> \u25cf Uses the werefalcons called the Distant Ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:10:17-07:00","id":1383569,"title":"","content":"241) There's been a chunk of people who just up-&amp;-vanished recently. Tracking them down leads you to a small, rural town effectively cut off from civilization.<br /> Then you notice what you think could be a Minotaur. You're gonna need some bigger guns.<br /> \u25cf The &quot;Minotaur&quot; that the characters saw is a Baal Hadad in hybrid form. Of course, they don't know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:11:25-07:00","id":1383570,"title":"","content":"242) Every so often recently someone dies a grueling death. The corpses all wind being shredded like so much confetti. It's a mess.<br /> Investigating the victims histories reveals that every one of them was guilty of something. Abuse, drug dealing, rape, one was a serial killer.<br /> You are conflicted. Should you allow this because none of the victims were not good for the neighborhood? Or should you hunt this creature down, because they are still a killer &amp; might get it wrong one time? Please ignore the fact that you yourself are a killer &amp; that this may very well be you.<br /> \u25cf I wrote this with the creature being one of the Colony &amp; the hunters belonging to the Union, but it's not fixed in stone that they are, so change it if that works better for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:40:42-07:00","id":1384324,"title":"","content":"243) A friend of yours complains that they feel they're being stalked by toads, of all things. You attribute it to stress, they're under a lot of it at the moment.<br /> A week later, you meet your friend again, &amp; something's different about them. Their skin has become unpleasantly dry to the touch, &amp; their stomach has begun to bloat. They've started acting greedy &amp; slothful.<br /> You have a bad feeling that you made a big mistake.<br /> \u25cf Hunters versus the Toad Host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:44:14-07:00","id":1384326,"title":"","content":"244) Your cell is approached by a demon. It claims that it desires to be a servant of the &quot;true God&quot; as opposed to the &quot;machine one&quot; that gave birth to it, but it doesn't know where to begin in making this so. It has requested your help in the matter.<br /> \u25cf I feel that this hook would require that your cell has a connection to one of the compacts or conspiracies of Christian nature (the Long Night, Malleus Maleficarum, Knights of St George, Order of St Anthony?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:45:02-07:00","id":1384328,"title":"","content":"245) Some fascistic movement is going to have a big event in your area. Given that 90% of your cell, at minimum, ascribes to the Antifa philosophy you're going to engage in some kind of counter-event. Especially when you learn that there might be a monster of some kind hiding among the fascists.<br /> \u25cf For an accurate, er, dissection of Antifa look to The Philosophy of Antifa by Philosophy Tube. Warning: the video is 1hr, 7mins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T18:59:21-07:00","id":1386227,"title":"","content":"246) Members of the Office of the Lord Stewards that are attached to a British embassy. Dealing with local supernatural stuff in the usual way the Office does, or at least trying to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:36:18-07:00","id":1391443,"title":"","content":"247) Your cell has starts getting sent on Black Book assignments. You have no idea why &amp; it's getting rather dangerous. When you investigate the matter (in between the Black Book assignments of course), you find that your cell is somehow stuck on getting these assignments &amp; no amount of bureaucracy can get you free.<br /> \u25cf Uses TFV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:53:16-07:00","id":1391611,"title":"","content":"248) A member of the Chosen of Krull recently acquired a large number of eldritch texts &amp; decided to study them &amp; find more Abyssal Blessings.<br /> They weren't as careful as they should have been, &amp; now an eldritch horror is building a power base under the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:54:56-07:00","id":1391612,"title":"","content":"249) &quot;Hello, this is Richard Mathers, warrior of God, member of the Malleus Maleficarum. Today I am performing a Benediction that I myself have uncovered, for the first time. I am doing this to prove that it works &amp; can be taught to the rest of order. The Benediction invokes the saint known as Bernward of Hildesheim &amp; it distorts spatial dimensions.&quot;<br /> The Malleus Maleficarum got that transmission a little over a day ago. When communications coming out of the building went silent, they sent in a team to find out what was going on. The team came back speaking of hallways that went on forever, massive rooms crossed in a single step, &amp; other unsettling spatial phenomena.<br /> For whatever reason, the Malleus Maleficarum has turned to your cell. You are to go in, return the building to its original dimensions, figure out what happened, determine whether or not the Benediction is safe for use, &amp; extract any survivors.<br /> May God keep you safe, for it looks like no one else will be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:55:28-07:00","id":1391613,"title":"","content":"250) A couple members of the Lucifuge went into guided meditation through the genetic memories of their demonic ancestors. Something went wrong &amp; when the mentor &quot;surfaced&quot;, the pupil didn't surface with them.<br /> It's now been over 24 hrs &amp; the Lady of Milan is for reason is getting desperate. Your task is to retrieve the pupil from the dreamstate, with or without a Castigation. The Lady of Milan has explicitly stated that if you succeed she will owe you one favour. As you prepare for the descent of sorts, the mentor comes to you &amp; informs you that the Recovered Memory appeared to be from somewhere or somewhen during the War in Heaven.<br /> If you aren't successfully at this, the Lady of Milan says she will have no choice but to kill the pupil.<br /> \u25cf R&amp;D, Castigation, Recovered Memory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:56:08-07:00","id":1391614,"title":"","content":"251) You're a member of the Lucifuge &amp; recently got your hands on a book considered part of the so-called &quot;Devil's Library&quot;. Once you confirmed all this you immediately started trawling through it for a new Castigation.<br /> And then it got stolen. And then you begin to feel weak. Turns out when you started uncovering one of the Castigations held between its covers, you instigated some sort of enchantment that drains your life force should you lose possession of it. The only way to break the enchantment is to finish uncovering the Castigation, but the clock is ticking.<br /> Tick tick tick tick.<br /> \u25cf R&amp;D, Castigation, The Devil's Library","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:56:38-07:00","id":1391616,"title":"","content":"252) Your cell comes upon a member of the Lucifuge. This hunter has the unfortunate habit of making multiple deals with demons in search of new Castigations.<br /> Now whilst the providing the Lucifuge with a plethora of new Castigations is a good thing, the near constant demon deals is taking a significant toll on the hunter's morality.<br /> The latest demon they've summoned has demand a child sacrifice &amp; the hunter is thinking about whether they should go through with it.<br /> \u25cf This Lucifuge member should have a deep understanding of numerous Castigations &amp; the majority of Castigations that they wield should be new ones they've learnt via the demon deals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:58:48-07:00","id":1391617,"title":"","content":"253) You are a member of the Cheiron Group &amp; have a close friend in one of the members of the Peleus Guild.<br /> You are called in one day. You friend in the Peleus Guild has been attacked. Apparently it was in retaliation of some hunt that you led. You must respond to this attack on your friend, after all if you don't then you don't really have the right to call yourself their friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T23:35:35-07:00","id":1398292,"title":"","content":"<b>254) </b>Your cell has kept in contact with another hunter cell which protects lower income neighborhoods and clear out the horrors which lurk in desolate industrial parks and abandoned warehouses. One day you lose contact with them, and three days later a deliver-in-case-you-don't-hear-from-me contingency &quot;if you're reading this we're likely dead&quot; message arrives to your Cell's point of contact for them. It details several of the creatures the other cell was researching and stalking, along with contact information for the cell members' families and a request to investigate the cause of their disappearance/death, finish their remaining cases, and look out for the safety of their family so that monsters don't get them.<br /> <br /> Among the cases, phenomena, and creatures they were investigating (use a few of the monster focused adventure hooks here, it is important for this story the cell is offered a lot more information and options to follow than normal) there is also a set of abandoned office buildings with transients disappearing without any trace, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1274149#post1274149\">caused by this</a>. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The Hungry Door to Nowhere has <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1170202#post1170202\">a Dimensional Shambler as a parasite</a> within its Tumor of Nowhere Cells, slowly stealing kills and the Hungry Doorway to Nowhere swallowed up all the members of the missing Hunter Cell in an attempt to get rid of the Dimensional Shambler. Also the family members of the other cell are likely to run afoul of the cells other cases, in particular unrelated vampire intrigue without the Cell being rescued or the player's taking over and cleaning up the loose ends. </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=154625#post154625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11. The Brotherhood of St. Athanasius discover a Benediction petitioning Saint Barbara.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a former member of an Artillery Military Occupational Specialty, this made me smile because I know whom Saint Barbara is and that'd be Awesome! Boom goes the prayer.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-23-2020, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T07:55:01-07:00","id":1412848,"title":"","content":"255: (Loyalists of Thule) A Japanese professor of folklore has made some waves in academic circles recently, claiming mankind's folklore all comes from the same root origin. While no one takes him seriously (Partly his theories, partly his abrasiveness), you know a possible asset when you see it. Find this professor, and see what he might have.<br /> <br /> (Based on the manga &quot;The Casefiles of Prof. Munakata&quot;)<br /> <br /> 256: (Union) You're hearing some weird shit outta Pittsburgh. The city's got a reputation for having some ugly monsters in it, but they aren't always trouble. At least they weren't. Word's coming in a bunch of honest-to-God hunchbacks with magic are trying to restart a steel mill. So what's the problem? Whoever's funding it doesn't want to hire any regular humans. Plus, people are bound to start asking questions when they see the workforce. Go to this mill, see what's happening, and figure out if you can't use this as a chance to help the regular working people of Pittsburgh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 09-11-2020, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T00:17:51-08:00","id":1425324,"title":"","content":"257: Your cell comes upon some monsters that have kidnapped a group of children. You go in, kill the monsters, &amp; return the children to their homes.<br /> What you didn't know was that the children had monsters among their family. Monsters who were either unaware of the kidnappings or were in the process of coming up with their own strategies to deal with this. They are now eternally grateful for your actions.<br /> How do you proceed with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:31:45-07:00","id":1466065,"title":"","content":"258: Evidence has come to your cell's attention that the local police precinct is dominated by slashers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}